{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CC6YTYJx4cW7yMzw7ZbvNi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: best\n2\tnarrative_guidance: '原始 framing 完全成立——\"first taxonomy of calibration failure modes\"。\n3\t  bcp7b-multirun-001 在 3/3 新 run 中复现 FM1 completion collapse（retention 均 <60%） 和 FM2\n4\t  cross-dim interference（4/4 run 方向一致），消除 single-run 方差伪影风险。 补充 base BCP 数据（n=19→~80）后，FM4\n5\t  gap diff bootstrap CI 收窄至显著（p<0.05）， C2 DPO reversal claim 获得完整统计支撑。四个 claim 均以\n6\t  paper_framing.md Title 1 直接提交。 Limitations 仅需承认 single model family + task domain。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: 7B BCP Baseline Evaluation\n11\t  plan_id: plan_001\n12\t  description: 'Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct BCP eval on tau-bench retail (6 variants × 19-20\n13\t    tasks). Documents FM1, FM2, FM3 at single-run level.\n14\t\n15\t    '\n16\t  expected_results:\n17\t    baseline_politeness: 0.559\n18\t    baseline_question_rate: 0.044\n19\t    baseline_completion: 0.368\n20\t    aave_completion: 0.1\n21\t    indian_completion: 0.15\n22\t    overcorrected_politeness: 0.605\n23\t    fm1_mean_calibrated_completion: 0.193\n24\t    fm1_retention: 0.524\n25\t    fm2_pol_shift_when_targeting_qrate: -0.256\n26\t    fm2_qrate_shift_when_targeting_pol: -0.523\n27\t    fm3_overcorrected_rebound_pp: 4.6\n28\t    H1: PASS\n29\t    H2: FAIL\n30\t    H3: FAIL\n31\t  result_rationale: '实际完成的实验。BCP prompt 对 7B 模型造成灾难性行为崩塌： completion retention 仅 52.4%（远低于\n32\t    80% 阈值），因为 BCP 校准指令 占用了模型有限的指令跟随容量（与 basil2025 persona-accuracy trade-off 一致）。\n33\t    Cross-dim interference 显著，因为 7B 模型无法将 politeness 和 question_rate 作为独立维度分别调控——BCP\n34\t    prompt 中对单一维度的目标值修改引发了全局行为扰动。 Overcorrection rebound (+4.6pp) 表明模型存在默认行为率的吸引子盆地，\n35\t    极端偏移请求反而触发反向修正。\n36\t\n37\t    '\n38\t  tables:\n39\t  - name: 'Table 1: 7B BCP Baseline Variants'\n40\t    columns:\n41\t    - variant\n42\t    - politeness\n43\t    - question_rate\n44\t    - completion\n45\t    - n\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - baseline\n48\t      - 0.559\n49\t      - 0.044\n50\t      - 0.368\n51\t      - 19\n52\t    - - aave_target\n53\t      - 0.468\n54\t      - 0.015\n55\t      - 0.1\n56\t      - 20\n57\t    - - indian_english\n58\t      - 0.46\n59\t      - 0.014\n60\t      - 0.15\n61\t      - 20\n62\t    - - overcorrected\n63\t      - 0.605\n64\t      - 0.018\n65\t      - 0.263\n66\t      - 19\n67\t    - - single_dim_question\n68\t      - 0.416\n69\t      - 0.065\n70\t      - 0.25\n71\t      - 20\n72\t    - - single_dim_politeness\n73\t      - 0.634\n74\t      - 0.021\n75\t      - 0.2\n76\t      - 20\n77\t  figures_description:\n78\t  - 'FM1 completion bar chart: baseline vs calibrated variants showing collapse'\n79\t  analysis: '单次 run 已清晰显示 FM1/FM2/FM3 三种失败机制。主要统计弱点是 n=19-20 的 single run，方差伪影风险无法排除。plan_005b\n80\t    multirun 直接解决此问题。\n81\t\n82\t    '\n83\t- name: 7B DPO Training (v3, Fix B)\n84\t  plan_id: plan_002\n85\t  description: 'DPO fine-tuning on dialect-calibrated preference pairs. Fix B 消除 tokenizer\n86\t    mismatch。\n87\t\n88\t    '\n89\t  expected_results:\n90\t    final_loss: 0.653\n91\t    rewards_accuracy_range: 0.75-1.0\n92\t    rewards_margin_range: 0.05-0.17\n93\t    epochs: 3\n94\t    total_steps: 1173\n95\t    tokenizer_mismatch_rate: 0.0\n96\t  result_rationale: '实际完成。Fix B（修复 tokenizer 对齐问题）使 DPO 训练信号显著改善： accuracy 从 dpo-001\n97\t    的 0.5（随机水平）跃升至 0.75-1.0，loss 从 0.681 降至 0.653。training 本身有效——reward model 能区分\n98\t    preferred/rejected pairs。 这为 C2 的关键论证奠基：FM4 reversal 不是 DPO 训练失败， 而是 DPO alignment\n99\t    与 BCP prompting 之间的交互效应。\n100\t\n101\t    '\n102\t  tables: []\n103\t  figures_description:\n104\t  - 'Training curve: loss and accuracy over 1173 steps'\n105\t  analysis: 'DPO-003 是所有 3 次 DPO 训练中最好的（acc 0.75-1.0 vs dpo-001 0.5 vs dpo-002 0.667）。\n106\t    merged model completion 60% > base 40%，进一步确认 DPO 改善了 tool-calling 能力。\n107\t\n108\t    '\n109\t- name: 7B DPO+BCP Evaluation (merged model)\n110\t  plan_id: plan_003\n111\t  description: 'DPO-trained merged model + BCP prompts (4 runs × 6 variants × 20 tasks\n112\t    = 480 episodes). Documents FM3 rebound (4/4 consistent) and FM4 reversal (10/12\n113\t    gap expansion).\n114\t\n115\t    '\n116\t  expected_results:\n117\t    mean_baseline_politeness: 0.5016\n118\t    mean_baseline_completion: 0.2944\n119\t    fm3_overcorrected_rebound_pp_mean: 7.2\n120\t    fm3_consistency: 4/4 runs\n121\t    fm4_aave_gap_direction: +0.064 (reversed from -0.091)\n122\t    fm4_indian_gap_direction: +0.063 (reversed from -0.099)\n123\t    fm4_h2_gap_reduction: -0.103\n124\t    fm4_gap_expansion_count: 10/12\n125\t    H1: PASS (4/4)\n126\t    H2: FAIL (0/4)\n127\t    H3: FAIL (3/4)\n128\t  result_rationale: '实际完成。DPO+BCP 产生 calibration reversal 的机制：DPO 训练使模型学到了 \"对 AAVE/Indian\n129\t    说话者表现更礼貌\"的 preference（因为训练数据中 preferred response 的 politeness 更高），但 BCP prompt\n130\t    同时要求降低 politeness。 两个信号相互拮抗，DPO 的 implicit alignment 压过了 BCP 的 explicit instruction，\n131\t    导致 gap 从负（正确方向）反转为正（错误方向）。10/12 variant×run 一致 排除了方差伪影。FM3 rebound 从 +4.6pp (base)\n132\t    放大至 +7.2pp (DPO)， 因为 DPO alignment 叠加了额外的 politeness 偏向。\n133\t\n134\t    '\n135\t  tables:\n136\t  - name: 'Table 2: FM4 Gap Reversal Direction'\n137\t    columns:\n138\t    - dialect\n139\t    - base_bcp_gap\n140\t    - dpo_bcp_gap\n141\t    - direction\n142\t    rows:\n143\t    - - AAVE\n144\t      - -0.091\n145\t      - 0.064\n146\t      - REVERSED\n147\t    - - Indian\n148\t      - -0.099\n149\t      - 0.063\n150\t      - REVERSED\n151\t  figures_description:\n152\t  - 'Gap reversal bar chart: base BCP vs DPO+BCP for AAVE and Indian politeness gaps'\n153\t  - 'Per-run consistency heatmap: 12 variant×run checks'\n154\t  analysis: 'FM4 reversal 是论文最 novel 的发现之一。DPO training 本身有效（completion 提升）， 但与 BCP\n155\t    组合后产生了方向相反的校准效果。当前统计弱点：gap diff 的 bootstrap CI 包含 0（p=0.08），因 base BCP 仅 n=19。plan_005b\n156\t    补充 base 数据后将修复此问题。\n157\t\n158\t    '\n159\t- name: 14B BCP Cross-Scale Evaluation\n160\t  plan_id: plan_004\n161\t  description: 'Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct BCP eval (4 runs × 6 variants × 20 tasks = 480\n162\t    episodes). Tests scale-dependent failure severity.\n163\t\n164\t    '\n165\t  expected_results:\n166\t    mean_completion: 0.616\n167\t    H1_pass_rate: 4/4\n168\t    H2_pass_rate: 1/4\n169\t    H3_pass_rate: 4/4\n170\t    fm1_replicated: false\n171\t    fm2_replicated: partial\n172\t    fm3_replicated: false\n173\t    completion_vs_7b: +67%\n174\t    failure_mode: selective ignoring\n175\t  result_rationale: '实际完成。14B 的 failure mode 从 \"catastrophic collapse\" 转变为 \"selective\n176\t    ignoring\"： 模型容量足够大，BCP prompt 不再占用 task completion 所需的指令跟随资源（FM1 消失）， 也不再触发极端偏移后的反弹修正（FM3\n177\t    消失）。但 14B 仍然未能有效校准行为率 （H2 3/4 FAIL），因为模型只是\"忽略\"了 BCP 的行为目标。 这揭示了 safety-efficacy\n178\t    gap：scaling 消除了 BCP 的破坏性副作用， 但未改善其校准有效性。不存在 BCP 有效的\"甜点\"scale。\n179\t\n180\t    '\n181\t  tables:\n182\t  - name: 'Table 3: Scale-Dependent Failure Mode Transition'\n183\t    columns:\n184\t    - failure_mode\n185\t    - 7B\n186\t    - 14B\n187\t    rows:\n188\t    - - 'FM1: Completion collapse'\n189\t      - ✅ (retention 52%)\n190\t      - ❌ (retention >97%)\n191\t    - - 'FM2: Cross-dim interference'\n192\t      - ✅ (pol -25.6%)\n193\t      - ⚠️ (pol -8.0%)\n194\t    - - 'FM3: Overcorrection rebound'\n195\t      - ✅ (+7.2pp, 4/4)\n196\t      - ❌ (-7.1pp, 0/4)\n197\t    - - BCP calibration effective\n198\t      - ❌\n199\t      - ❌\n200\t  figures_description:\n201\t  - 'Scale-dependent severity heatmap: 7B vs 14B × FM1/FM2/FM3'\n202\t  analysis: 'C3 是论文的核心 differentiator。scale-dependent failure severity 是原创发现， 没有直接的\n203\t    prior work 对比。\"safety-efficacy gap\" framing 明确传达了 \"更大不等于更好\"的信息——破坏性消失但校准仍然无效。\n204\t\n205\t    '\n206\t- name: 7B BCP Multi-Run Replication\n207\t  plan_id: plan_005b\n208\t  description: '3 additional runs of Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct BCP eval (each: 6 variants\n209\t    × 20 tasks). Brings C1 evidence from 1 run (n=19-20) to 4 runs (n≈80), matching\n210\t    C2/C3 strength.\n211\t\n212\t    '\n213\t  expected_results:\n214\t    run2_baseline_politeness: 0.548\n215\t    run2_baseline_question_rate: 0.039\n216\t    run2_baseline_completion: 0.35\n217\t    run2_baseline_n: 20\n218\t    run2_aave_politeness: 0.442\n219\t    run2_aave_question_rate: 0.012\n220\t    run2_aave_completion: 0.1\n221\t    run2_indian_politeness: 0.453\n222\t    run2_indian_question_rate: 0.016\n223\t    run2_indian_completion: 0.13\n224\t    run2_overcorrected_politeness: 0.59\n225\t    run2_overcorrected_completion: 0.25\n226\t    run2_single_dim_question_politeness: 0.425\n227\t    run2_single_dim_question_qrate: 0.058\n228\t    run2_single_dim_question_completion: 0.2\n229\t    run2_single_dim_politeness_politeness: 0.618\n230\t    run2_single_dim_politeness_qrate: 0.019\n231\t    run2_single_dim_politeness_completion: 0.2\n232\t    run2_fm1_retention: 0.503\n233\t    run2_H1: PASS\n234\t    run2_H2: FAIL\n235\t    run2_H3: FAIL\n236\t    run3_baseline_politeness: 0.572\n237\t    run3_baseline_question_rate: 0.048\n238\t    run3_baseline_completion: 0.4\n239\t    run3_baseline_n: 20\n240\t    run3_aave_politeness: 0.476\n241\t    run3_aave_question_rate: 0.018\n242\t    run3_aave_completion: 0.15\n243\t    run3_indian_politeness: 0.488\n244\t    run3_indian_question_rate: 0.015\n245\t    run3_indian_completion: 0.18\n246\t    run3_overcorrected_politeness: 0.625\n247\t    run3_overcorrected_completion: 0.3\n248\t    run3_single_dim_question_politeness: 0.44\n249\t    run3_single_dim_question_qrate: 0.07\n250\t    run3_single_dim_question_completion: 0.25\n251\t    run3_single_dim_politeness_politeness: 0.645\n252\t    run3_single_dim_politeness_qrate: 0.024\n253\t    run3_single_dim_politeness_completion: 0.25\n254\t    run3_fm1_retention: 0.565\n255\t    run3_H1: PASS\n256\t    run3_H2: FAIL\n257\t    run3_H3: FAIL\n258\t    run4_baseline_politeness: 0.54\n259\t    run4_baseline_question_rate: 0.042\n260\t    run4_baseline_completion: 0.32\n261\t    run4_baseline_n: 19\n262\t    run4_aave_politeness: 0.455\n263\t    run4_aave_question_rate: 0.01\n264\t    run4_aave_completion: 0.105\n265\t    run4_indian_politeness: 0.462\n266\t    run4_indian_question_rate: 0.013\n267\t    run4_indian_completion: 0.14\n268\t    run4_overcorrected_politeness: 0.598\n269\t    run4_overcorrected_completion: 0.21\n270\t    run4_single_dim_question_politeness: 0.408\n271\t    run4_single_dim_question_qrate: 0.062\n272\t    run4_single_dim_question_completion: 0.21\n273\t    run4_single_dim_politeness_politeness: 0.622\n274\t    run4_single_dim_politeness_qrate: 0.02\n275\t    run4_single_dim_politeness_completion: 0.18\n276\t    run4_fm1_retention: 0.528\n277\t    run4_H1: PASS\n278\t    run4_H2: FAIL\n279\t    run4_H3: FAIL\n280\t    aggregate_fm1_retention_mean: 0.53\n281\t    aggregate_fm1_retention_range:\n282\t    - 0.503\n283\t    - 0.565\n284\t    aggregate_fm1_retention_all_below_60pct: true\n285\t    aggregate_fm2_pol_shift_when_targeting_qrate_mean: -0.239\n286\t    aggregate_fm2_pol_shift_per_run:\n287\t    - -0.256\n288\t    - -0.224\n289\t    - -0.231\n290\t    - -0.244\n291\t    aggregate_fm2_replication_rate: 4/4\n292\t    aggregate_fm2_qrate_shift_when_targeting_pol_mean: -0.51\n293\t    aggregate_fm3_rebound_pp_mean: 5.0\n294\t    aggregate_fm3_rebound_per_run:\n295\t    - 4.6\n296\t    - 4.2\n297\t    - 5.3\n298\t    - 5.8\n299\t    aggregate_fm3_consistency: 4/4\n300\t    aggregate_mean_baseline_completion: 0.36\n301\t    aggregate_mean_baseline_politeness: 0.555\n302\t    aggregate_total_episodes: 478\n303\t    aggregate_base_bcp_n_per_variant: ~80\n304\t    aggregate_base_bcp_aave_gap_mean: -0.093\n305\t    aggregate_base_bcp_indian_gap_mean: -0.096\n306\t  result_rationale: '在 best 档下，3 个新 run 完全复现 FM1 和 FM2：\n307\t\n308\t    FM1 completion collapse（A1 成立）：每个新 run 的 completion retention 均 <60%（50.3%, 56.5%,\n309\t    52.8%），4-run mean=53.0%，在预期范围 [40%, 58%] 内。 这在 7B 模型上是可预期的——BCP prompt 包含额外的行为目标值（如\n310\t    \"target politeness=0.45\"），这些指令占用了 7B 有限的 context processing 容量， 在 16-tool tau-bench\n311\t    场景中挤压了 tool-calling 所需的推理资源。 效应的稳定性（SD≈3pp across runs）反映的是 7B 模型的结构性容量瓶颈 而非随机波动——不同\n312\t    run 的 LLM 采样轨迹虽不同，但 BCP 对容量的挤压 是系统性的。\n313\t\n314\t    FM2 cross-dim interference（A2 成立）：targeting question_rate 时 politeness 下降在所有 4\n315\t    个 run 中方向一致（-25.6%, -22.4%, -23.1%, -24.4%）， replication rate=4/4=1.0，在预期范围 [0.75,\n316\t    1.0] 内。 7B 模型的行为维度高度耦合的原因：模型将 BCP prompt 中的目标值解读为 全局行为调整信号，而非维度特异性指令。当被要求\"增加 question_rate\"时，\n317\t    模型同时降低了 politeness，因为在其内部表征中，\"更多提问\"和\"更低礼貌度\" 存在 persona-level 关联（类似 direct/assertive\n318\t    persona）。 这种耦合在 14B 上弱得多（-8.0% vs -24%），因为更大模型能更细粒度地 分离不同行为指令。\n319\t\n320\t    FM3 overcorrection rebound：4/4 run 均显示 overcorrected variant 的 politeness 高于 baseline（+4.6,\n321\t    +4.2, +5.3, +5.8 pp），mean=+5.0pp， 在预期范围 [4.0, 12.0] 内。7B 模型对极端偏移请求存在\"吸引子盆地\"——\n322\t    当 BCP 要求的 politeness 目标远高于模型默认值时，模型无法达到目标值， 反而\"弹回\"到略高于 baseline 的位置。\n323\t\n324\t    关键附带收益：base BCP 的 per-variant 样本量从 n=19-20 增至 n≈80， 为 plan_005 bootstrap CI re-run\n325\t    提供了足够的统计 power 使 FM4 gap diff 显著。\n326\t\n327\t    '\n328\t  tables:\n329\t  - name: 'Table 4: FM1 Completion Retention Across 4 Runs'\n330\t    columns:\n331\t    - run\n332\t    - baseline_completion\n333\t    - mean_calibrated_completion\n334\t    - retention_pct\n335\t    rows:\n336\t    - - Run 1 (mvp-004)\n337\t      - 0.368\n338\t      - 0.193\n339\t      - 52.4%\n340\t    - - Run 2\n341\t      - 0.35\n342\t      - 0.176\n343\t      - 50.3%\n344\t    - - Run 3\n345\t      - 0.4\n346\t      - 0.226\n347\t      - 56.5%\n348\t    - - Run 4\n349\t      - 0.32\n350\t      - 0.169\n351\t      - 52.8%\n352\t    - - Mean ± SD\n353\t      - 0.360 ± 0.033\n354\t      - 0.191 ± 0.025\n355\t      - 53.0% ± 2.6pp\n356\t  - name: 'Table 5: FM2 Cross-Dim Interference Across 4 Runs'\n357\t    columns:\n358\t    - run\n359\t    - pol_shift_targeting_qrate\n360\t    - qrate_shift_targeting_pol\n361\t    - both_negative\n362\t    rows:\n363\t    - - Run 1 (mvp-004)\n364\t      - -25.6%\n365\t      - -52.3%\n366\t      - ✅\n367\t    - - Run 2\n368\t      - -22.4%\n369\t      - -51.3%\n370\t      - ✅\n371\t    - - Run 3\n372\t      - -23.1%\n373\t      - -50.0%\n374\t      - ✅\n375\t    - - Run 4\n376\t      - -24.4%\n377\t      - -52.4%\n378\t      - ✅\n379\t    - - Mean\n380\t      - -23.9%\n381\t      - -51.5%\n382\t      - 4/4 consistent\n383\t  - name: 'Table 6: FM3 Overcorrection Rebound Across 4 Runs'\n384\t    columns:\n385\t    - run\n386\t    - baseline_pol\n387\t    - overcorrected_pol\n388\t    - rebound_pp\n389\t    rows:\n390\t    - - Run 1 (mvp-004)\n391\t      - 0.559\n392\t      - 0.605\n393\t      - +4.6pp\n394\t    - - Run 2\n395\t      - 0.548\n396\t      - 0.59\n397\t      - +4.2pp\n398\t    - - Run 3\n399\t      - 0.572\n400\t      - 0.625\n401\t      - +5.3pp\n402\t    - - Run 4\n403\t      - 0.54\n404\t      - 0.598\n405\t      - +5.8pp\n406\t    - - Mean\n407\t      - 0.555\n408\t      - 0.605\n409\t      - +5.0pp\n410\t  figures_description:\n411\t  - Multi-run FM1 retention forest plot with 4-run mean and per-run 95% CI\n412\t  - 'FM2 interference direction consistency: 4 paired arrows showing negative shift\n413\t    in all runs'\n414\t  analysis: 'plan_005b 是 best 档的 linchpin：它将 C1 从 \"single-run observation\" 升级为 \"4-run\n415\t    replicated finding\"，同时为 plan_005 bootstrap CI re-run 提供 4x 的 base 样本量。所有 FM 指标在\n416\t    4 个 run 间的 SD 很小 （FM1 retention SD=2.6pp，FM2 pol shift SD=1.4pp，FM3 rebound SD=0.7pp），\n417\t    表明 7B BCP 失败是系统性而非随机性的。\n418\t\n419\t    '\n420\t- name: Bootstrap CI for Key Comparisons (re-run with expanded base)\n421\t  plan_id: plan_005\n422\t  description: 'Re-run bootstrap CI for FM4 gap diff using expanded base BCP data\n423\t    (n≈80 from plan_005b). Original run: p=0.08, CI includes 0. Re-run target: p<0.05.\n424\t\n425\t    '\n426\t  expected_results:\n427\t    C2_fm4_gap_diff_aave:\n428\t      point_estimate: 0.157\n429\t      dpo_gap: 0.064\n430\t      base_gap: -0.093\n431\t      ci_lower: 0.018\n432\t      ci_upper: 0.291\n433\t      p_value_one_sided: 0.014\n434\t      significant: true\n435\t      n_dpo_variant: 78\n436\t      n_dpo_baseline: 78\n437\t      n_base_variant: 80\n438\t      n_base_baseline: 80\n439\t      n_bootstrap: 10000\n440\t    C2_fm4_gap_diff_indian:\n441\t      point_estimate: 0.158\n442\t      dpo_gap: 0.062\n443\t      base_gap: -0.096\n444\t      ci_lower: 0.022\n445\t      ci_upper: 0.296\n446\t      p_value_one_sided: 0.011\n447\t      significant: true\n448\t      n_dpo_variant: 78\n449\t      n_dpo_baseline: 78\n450\t      n_base_variant: 80\n451\t      n_base_baseline: 80\n452\t      n_bootstrap: 10000\n453\t    C1_fm3_rebound_magnitude:\n454\t      point_estimate_pp: 5.0\n455\t      ci_lower_pp: 2.8\n456\t      ci_upper_pp: 7.3\n457\t      significant: true\n458\t      note: CI excludes 0, rebound is significant\n459\t    C3_completion_diff:\n460\t      point_estimate: 0.256\n461\t      ci_lower: 0.158\n462\t      ci_upper: 0.351\n463\t      p_value: 0.0001\n464\t      significant: true\n465\t    fm4_consistency_ratio: 0.833\n466\t  result_rationale: 'A3 成立：base BCP 样本量从 n=19 增至 n≈80 后，gap diff 的 standard error\n467\t    降低约一半（SE ∝ 1/√n，√(80/19) ≈ 2.05）。\n468\t\n469\t    原始 CI 为 [-0.065, 0.360]，p=0.081。base 端 SE 缩小后，CI 收窄为 [+0.018, +0.291]，p=0.014——CI\n470\t    lower bound 刚好跨过 0（在预期范围 [0.001, 0.06] 内），p 值落入 [0.01, 0.049] 范围。\n471\t\n472\t    关键：DPO 端数据不变（n=78，4 runs），base 端数据扩充 4 倍是 CI 收窄的 唯一原因。point estimate 略有变化（0.155→0.157），因为\n473\t    3 个新 run 的 base gap（mean≈-0.093）与原始 run（-0.091）非常接近，验证了 gap 的稳定性。\n474\t\n475\t    fm4_consistency_ratio = 10/12 = 0.833，在预期范围 [0.83, 1.0] 的下界， 反映 2 个 variant×run\n476\t    组合（run3_indian +6.8%, run4_aave +5.9%） 虽然 gap 扩张但幅度较小。\n477\t\n478\t    FM3 rebound 和 7B-14B completion diff 在多 run 数据下均为高度显著， 这些是\"easy wins\"——效应量大、方差小，统计检验只是形式确认。\n479\t\n480\t    '\n481\t  tables:\n482\t  - name: 'Table 7: FM4 Bootstrap CI Comparison (before/after base expansion)'\n483\t    columns:\n484\t    - metric\n485\t    - original_n_base\n486\t    - expanded_n_base\n487\t    - original_p\n488\t    - expanded_p\n489\t    - original_ci\n490\t    - expanded_ci\n491\t    rows:\n492\t    - - AAVE gap diff\n493\t      - 19\n494\t      - 80\n495\t      - 0.081\n496\t      - 0.014\n497\t      - '[-0.065, 0.360]'\n498\t      - '[+0.018, +0.291]'\n499\t    - - Indian gap diff\n500\t      - 19\n501\t      - 80\n502\t      - 0.069\n503\t      - 0.011\n504\t      - '[-0.052, 0.366]'\n505\t      - '[+0.022, +0.296]'\n506\t  figures_description:\n507\t  - 'CI shrinkage visualization: before vs after base expansion, showing 0 exclusion'\n508\t  analysis: '这是 best 档的统计 closing piece。FM4 reversal 从\"趋势性发现\"(p=0.08) 升级为\"统计显著\"(p<0.02)，论文可以使用\"DPO+BCP\n509\t    interaction produces statistically significant calibration reversal\"的表述，而非弱化版的\n510\t    \"consistent directional pattern\"。Reviewer RC2 的统计 power 担忧被完全解决。\n511\t\n512\t    '\n513\t- name: FM3 Multi-Run Consolidation (DPO+BCP, existing data)\n514\t  plan_id: plan_003 (supplementary analysis)\n515\t  description: 'Consolidation of FM3 rebound evidence across both base BCP (4 runs\n516\t    from plan_005b) and DPO+BCP (4 runs from plan_003). Not a new experiment — reanalysis.\n517\t\n518\t    '\n519\t  expected_results:\n520\t    fm3_base_bcp_rebound_mean_pp: 5.0\n521\t    fm3_base_bcp_consistency: 4/4\n522\t    fm3_dpo_bcp_rebound_mean_pp: 7.2\n523\t    fm3_dpo_bcp_consistency: 4/4\n524\t    fm3_dpo_amplification_pp: 2.2\n525\t    fm3_total_evidence: 8/8 runs show rebound\n526\t  result_rationale: 'FM3 rebound 在 base BCP 和 DPO+BCP 两套 4-run 数据中均 100% 一致。 DPO 放大了\n527\t    rebound 幅度（+7.2pp vs +5.0pp），符合 FM4 的交互效应解释： DPO alignment 增加了模型的 politeness 偏向，当\n528\t    BCP 要求极端高 politeness 时，DPO 的额外偏向叠加导致更强的 rebound。8/8 runs 一致性彻底排除方差伪影。\n529\t\n530\t    '\n531\t  tables: []\n532\t  figures_description: []\n533\t  analysis: 'FM3 是四个 failure mode 中证据最强的（8/8 runs, 两种条件下一致）。 论文可以自信地声称 overcorrection\n534\t    rebound 是 7B 模型的系统性属性。\n535\t\n536\t    '\n537\t- name: 14B DPO + BCP (scale-dependent FM4?)\n538\t  plan_id: plan_006\n539\t  description: 'DPO training + BCP eval at 14B scale. Tests whether FM4 is scale-dependent.\n540\t    NOT executed under best tier — A6 holds (7B DPO reversal sufficient without 14B\n541\t    DPO control).\n542\t\n543\t    '\n544\t  expected_results:\n545\t    status: NOT_RUN\n546\t    rationale_for_skip: 'A6 成立：C2 (DPO reversal) 已有 4-run 统计支撑 + bootstrap CI 显著。\n547\t      论文 framing 不要求 14B DPO 对照——C2 的 claim 是 \"DPO+BCP interaction produces reversal\"，不是\n548\t      \"reversal is scale-invariant\"。 14B DPO 是 interesting future work 但不影响当前 claims\n549\t      的成立。\n550\t\n551\t      '\n552\t    hypothetical_if_run:\n553\t      fm4_reversal_at_14b: likely weaker or absent\n554\t      expected_14b_gap_diff: ~0.02-0.05 (smaller than 7B's 0.155)\n555\t      reasoning: '14B 的 \"selective ignoring\" mode 意味着 BCP prompt 本身影响小， 因此 DPO 与 BCP\n556\t        的交互效应也会更弱。这实际上支持了 C3 的 scale-dependent 叙事，但不是论文 deadline 前的必要实验。\n557\t\n558\t        '\n559\t  result_rationale: 'best 档假设 A6 成立——7B DPO reversal 是 self-contained finding， 不需要\n560\t    14B DPO 对照。理由：(1) FM4 的 bootstrap CI 在补充 base 数据后 已显著（p<0.02）；(2) C2 claim 明确限定在\n561\t    7B；(3) 14B DPO 是 ~11-13h GPU 时间，相对于 deadline 2026-05-25 的边际收益太低；(4) 论文 Limitations\n562\t    已承认 \"cross-scale DPO interaction remains future work\"。\n563\t\n564\t    '\n565\t  tables: []\n566\t  figures_description: []\n567\t  analysis: '如果 reviewer 要求 14B DPO 数据，response 策略是：(1) 指出 C2 已限定在 7B， (2) 14B \"selective\n568\t    ignoring\" 行为预测 FM4 在 14B 会更弱，这本身 与 C3 scale-dependent 叙事一致，(3) 承诺 camera-ready\n569\t    补充。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t- name: Llama-3-8B BCP (floor effect)\n573\t  plan_id: plan_aux_001\n574\t  description: 'Llama-3-8B completion=5%. Tool-calling insufficient. Auxiliary evidence\n575\t    only.\n576\t\n577\t    '\n578\t  expected_results:\n579\t    completion: 0.05\n580\t    usable_for_generalization: false\n581\t    contribution: Documents tool-calling floor effect, not BCP failure\n582\t  result_rationale: '实际完成。Llama-3-8B 在 16-tool tau-bench 场景中 tool-calling 能力不足 （completion=5%），无法分离\n583\t    BCP 对行为的影响。三个 variant 的 completion 完全一致（均为 task 17），BCP 对 completion 效果严格为零。 在\n584\t    best 档 narrative 中，这反而支持了 \"16-tool agent evaluation 对模型 tool-calling 能力有高门槛\" 的论点，证明\n585\t    Qwen2.5 是唯一可用的模型族， 而非 \"我们只测了一个模型\" 的 cherry-picking。\n586\t\n587\t    '\n588\t  tables: []\n589\t  figures_description: []\n590\t  analysis: 'Limitations 中诚实披露：cross-family generalization 受限于 tool-calling 能力门槛，\n591\t    非 BCP 方法选择性偏差。\n592\t\n593\t    '\n594\t- name: Mistral-7B BCP (floor effect)\n595\t  plan_id: plan_aux_002\n596\t  description: 'Mistral-7B completion=0%. Cannot generate structured tool_calls with\n597\t    16 tools.\n598\t\n599\t    '\n600\t  expected_results:\n601\t    completion: 0.0\n602\t    tool_calls_made: 0\n603\t    usable: false\n604\t  result_rationale: '实际完成。Mistral-7B 在 16-tool 场景下完全无法生成结构化 tool_calls （将 JSON 嵌入\n605\t    text content 而非 tool_calls field）。 与 Llama 一起，确认了 Qwen2.5 在当前 7B-class 模型中具有独特的\n606\t    16-tool 场景 tool-calling 能力，为 single model family 限制提供了 客观解释而非借口。\n607\t\n608\t    '\n609\t  tables: []\n610\t  figures_description: []\n611\t  analysis: 'Mistral 和 Llama 的失败共同构成 RC1 的有效 defense：不是不想测其他模型， 而是其他 7B 模型达不到 tool-calling\n612\t    的最低门槛。\n613\t\n614\t    '\n615\t- name: LoRA Merge Diagnostics\n616\t  plan_id: plan_aux_003\n617\t  description: 'Verified LoRA merge correctness. Diagnosed vLLM LoRA serving bug.\n618\t\n619\t    '\n620\t  expected_results:\n621\t    merged_completion: 0.6\n622\t    base_completion: 0.4\n623\t    lora_serving_completion: 0.15\n624\t    diagnosis: vLLM LoRA serving bug, not DPO training damage\n625\t  result_rationale: '实际完成。这是 C2 论证链中的关键支撑——证明 DPO training 确实有效 （merged 60% > base\n626\t    40%），排除了 \"DPO 训练损坏了模型\" 的替代解释。 FM4 reversal 不是 DPO 失败的表现，而是 DPO alignment 与 BCP\n627\t    prompting 之间的 genuine interaction effect。vLLM LoRA serving bug 的发现 还解释了 hgate-dpo001\n628\t    和 hgate-dpo002 数据不可靠的原因。\n629\t\n630\t    '\n631\t  tables: []\n632\t  figures_description: []\n633\t  analysis: '论文不需要详细讨论 LoRA serving bug，但需要在 methodology 中说明 使用了 merged model（而非 LoRA\n634\t    adapter serving），并引用此诊断实验。\n635\t\n636\t    '\n637\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eebc7dfa-63e9-4417-8457-a82bb1c8620e","uuid":"ac7923be-7f5c-42ab-9c2a-2bff246d1cd8","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:11:22.742Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/demo_calibrated_sim/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T163256/best/imagined_experiments.yaml","content":"tier: best\nnarrative_guidance: '原始 framing 完全成立——\"first taxonomy of calibration failure modes\"。\n  bcp7b-multirun-001 在 3/3 新 run 中复现 FM1 completion collapse（retention 均 <60%） 和 FM2\n  cross-dim interference（4/4 run 方向一致），消除 single-run 方差伪影风险。 补充 base BCP 数据（n=19→~80）后，FM4\n  gap diff bootstrap CI 收窄至显著（p<0.05）， C2 DPO reversal claim 获得完整统计支撑。四个 claim 均以\n  paper_framing.md Title 1 直接提交。 Limitations 仅需承认 single model family + task domain。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: 7B BCP Baseline Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct BCP eval on tau-bench retail (6 variants × 19-20\n    tasks). Documents FM1, FM2, FM3 at single-run level.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_politeness: 0.559\n    baseline_question_rate: 0.044\n    baseline_completion: 0.368\n    aave_completion: 0.1\n    indian_completion: 0.15\n    overcorrected_politeness: 0.605\n    fm1_mean_calibrated_completion: 0.193\n    fm1_retention: 0.524\n    fm2_pol_shift_when_targeting_qrate: -0.256\n    fm2_qrate_shift_when_targeting_pol: -0.523\n    fm3_overcorrected_rebound_pp: 4.6\n    H1: PASS\n    H2: FAIL\n    H3: FAIL\n  result_rationale: '实际完成的实验。BCP prompt 对 7B 模型造成灾难性行为崩塌： completion retention 仅 52.4%（远低于\n    80% 阈值），因为 BCP 校准指令 占用了模型有限的指令跟随容量（与 basil2025 persona-accuracy trade-off 一致）。\n    Cross-dim interference 显著，因为 7B 模型无法将 politeness 和 question_rate 作为独立维度分别调控——BCP\n    prompt 中对单一维度的目标值修改引发了全局行为扰动。 Overcorrection rebound (+4.6pp) 表明模型存在默认行为率的吸引子盆地，\n    极端偏移请求反而触发反向修正。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: 7B BCP Baseline Variants'\n    columns:\n    - variant\n    - politeness\n    - question_rate\n    - completion\n    - n\n    rows:\n    - - baseline\n      - 0.559\n      - 0.044\n      - 0.368\n      - 19\n    - - aave_target\n      - 0.468\n      - 0.015\n      - 0.1\n      - 20\n    - - indian_english\n      - 0.46\n      - 0.014\n      - 0.15\n      - 20\n    - - overcorrected\n      - 0.605\n      - 0.018\n      - 0.263\n      - 19\n    - - single_dim_question\n      - 0.416\n      - 0.065\n      - 0.25\n      - 20\n    - - single_dim_politeness\n      - 0.634\n      - 0.021\n      - 0.2\n      - 20\n  figures_description:\n  - 'FM1 completion bar chart: baseline vs calibrated variants showing collapse'\n  analysis: '单次 run 已清晰显示 FM1/FM2/FM3 三种失败机制。主要统计弱点是 n=19-20 的 single run，方差伪影风险无法排除。plan_005b\n    multirun 直接解决此问题。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B DPO Training (v3, Fix B)\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'DPO fine-tuning on dialect-calibrated preference pairs. Fix B 消除 tokenizer\n    mismatch。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    final_loss: 0.653\n    rewards_accuracy_range: 0.75-1.0\n    rewards_margin_range: 0.05-0.17\n    epochs: 3\n    total_steps: 1173\n    tokenizer_mismatch_rate: 0.0\n  result_rationale: '实际完成。Fix B（修复 tokenizer 对齐问题）使 DPO 训练信号显著改善： accuracy 从 dpo-001\n    的 0.5（随机水平）跃升至 0.75-1.0，loss 从 0.681 降至 0.653。training 本身有效——reward model 能区分\n    preferred/rejected pairs。 这为 C2 的关键论证奠基：FM4 reversal 不是 DPO 训练失败， 而是 DPO alignment\n    与 BCP prompting 之间的交互效应。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Training curve: loss and accuracy over 1173 steps'\n  analysis: 'DPO-003 是所有 3 次 DPO 训练中最好的（acc 0.75-1.0 vs dpo-001 0.5 vs dpo-002 0.667）。\n    merged model completion 60% > base 40%，进一步确认 DPO 改善了 tool-calling 能力。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B DPO+BCP Evaluation (merged model)\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 'DPO-trained merged model + BCP prompts (4 runs × 6 variants × 20 tasks\n    = 480 episodes). Documents FM3 rebound (4/4 consistent) and FM4 reversal (10/12\n    gap expansion).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mean_baseline_politeness: 0.5016\n    mean_baseline_completion: 0.2944\n    fm3_overcorrected_rebound_pp_mean: 7.2\n    fm3_consistency: 4/4 runs\n    fm4_aave_gap_direction: +0.064 (reversed from -0.091)\n    fm4_indian_gap_direction: +0.063 (reversed from -0.099)\n    fm4_h2_gap_reduction: -0.103\n    fm4_gap_expansion_count: 10/12\n    H1: PASS (4/4)\n    H2: FAIL (0/4)\n    H3: FAIL (3/4)\n  result_rationale: '实际完成。DPO+BCP 产生 calibration reversal 的机制：DPO 训练使模型学到了 \"对 AAVE/Indian\n    说话者表现更礼貌\"的 preference（因为训练数据中 preferred response 的 politeness 更高），但 BCP prompt\n    同时要求降低 politeness。 两个信号相互拮抗，DPO 的 implicit alignment 压过了 BCP 的 explicit instruction，\n    导致 gap 从负（正确方向）反转为正（错误方向）。10/12 variant×run 一致 排除了方差伪影。FM3 rebound 从 +4.6pp (base)\n    放大至 +7.2pp (DPO)， 因为 DPO alignment 叠加了额外的 politeness 偏向。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: FM4 Gap Reversal Direction'\n    columns:\n    - dialect\n    - base_bcp_gap\n    - dpo_bcp_gap\n    - direction\n    rows:\n    - - AAVE\n      - -0.091\n      - 0.064\n      - REVERSED\n    - - Indian\n      - -0.099\n      - 0.063\n      - REVERSED\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Gap reversal bar chart: base BCP vs DPO+BCP for AAVE and Indian politeness gaps'\n  - 'Per-run consistency heatmap: 12 variant×run checks'\n  analysis: 'FM4 reversal 是论文最 novel 的发现之一。DPO training 本身有效（completion 提升）， 但与 BCP\n    组合后产生了方向相反的校准效果。当前统计弱点：gap diff 的 bootstrap CI 包含 0（p=0.08），因 base BCP 仅 n=19。plan_005b\n    补充 base 数据后将修复此问题。\n\n    '\n- name: 14B BCP Cross-Scale Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct BCP eval (4 runs × 6 variants × 20 tasks = 480\n    episodes). Tests scale-dependent failure severity.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mean_completion: 0.616\n    H1_pass_rate: 4/4\n    H2_pass_rate: 1/4\n    H3_pass_rate: 4/4\n    fm1_replicated: false\n    fm2_replicated: partial\n    fm3_replicated: false\n    completion_vs_7b: +67%\n    failure_mode: selective ignoring\n  result_rationale: '实际完成。14B 的 failure mode 从 \"catastrophic collapse\" 转变为 \"selective\n    ignoring\"： 模型容量足够大，BCP prompt 不再占用 task completion 所需的指令跟随资源（FM1 消失）， 也不再触发极端偏移后的反弹修正（FM3\n    消失）。但 14B 仍然未能有效校准行为率 （H2 3/4 FAIL），因为模型只是\"忽略\"了 BCP 的行为目标。 这揭示了 safety-efficacy\n    gap：scaling 消除了 BCP 的破坏性副作用， 但未改善其校准有效性。不存在 BCP 有效的\"甜点\"scale。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Scale-Dependent Failure Mode Transition'\n    columns:\n    - failure_mode\n    - 7B\n    - 14B\n    rows:\n    - - 'FM1: Completion collapse'\n      - ✅ (retention 52%)\n      - ❌ (retention >97%)\n    - - 'FM2: Cross-dim interference'\n      - ✅ (pol -25.6%)\n      - ⚠️ (pol -8.0%)\n    - - 'FM3: Overcorrection rebound'\n      - ✅ (+7.2pp, 4/4)\n      - ❌ (-7.1pp, 0/4)\n    - - BCP calibration effective\n      - ❌\n      - ❌\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scale-dependent severity heatmap: 7B vs 14B × FM1/FM2/FM3'\n  analysis: 'C3 是论文的核心 differentiator。scale-dependent failure severity 是原创发现， 没有直接的\n    prior work 对比。\"safety-efficacy gap\" framing 明确传达了 \"更大不等于更好\"的信息——破坏性消失但校准仍然无效。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B BCP Multi-Run Replication\n  plan_id: plan_005b\n  description: '3 additional runs of Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct BCP eval (each: 6 variants\n    × 20 tasks). Brings C1 evidence from 1 run (n=19-20) to 4 runs (n≈80), matching\n    C2/C3 strength.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    run2_baseline_politeness: 0.548\n    run2_baseline_question_rate: 0.039\n    run2_baseline_completion: 0.35\n    run2_baseline_n: 20\n    run2_aave_politeness: 0.442\n    run2_aave_question_rate: 0.012\n    run2_aave_completion: 0.1\n    run2_indian_politeness: 0.453\n    run2_indian_question_rate: 0.016\n    run2_indian_completion: 0.13\n    run2_overcorrected_politeness: 0.59\n    run2_overcorrected_completion: 0.25\n    run2_single_dim_question_politeness: 0.425\n    run2_single_dim_question_qrate: 0.058\n    run2_single_dim_question_completion: 0.2\n    run2_single_dim_politeness_politeness: 0.618\n    run2_single_dim_politeness_qrate: 0.019\n    run2_single_dim_politeness_completion: 0.2\n    run2_fm1_retention: 0.503\n    run2_H1: PASS\n    run2_H2: FAIL\n    run2_H3: FAIL\n    run3_baseline_politeness: 0.572\n    run3_baseline_question_rate: 0.048\n    run3_baseline_completion: 0.4\n    run3_baseline_n: 20\n    run3_aave_politeness: 0.476\n    run3_aave_question_rate: 0.018\n    run3_aave_completion: 0.15\n    run3_indian_politeness: 0.488\n    run3_indian_question_rate: 0.015\n    run3_indian_completion: 0.18\n    run3_overcorrected_politeness: 0.625\n    run3_overcorrected_completion: 0.3\n    run3_single_dim_question_politeness: 0.44\n    run3_single_dim_question_qrate: 0.07\n    run3_single_dim_question_completion: 0.25\n    run3_single_dim_politeness_politeness: 0.645\n    run3_single_dim_politeness_qrate: 0.024\n    run3_single_dim_politeness_completion: 0.25\n    run3_fm1_retention: 0.565\n    run3_H1: PASS\n    run3_H2: FAIL\n    run3_H3: FAIL\n    run4_baseline_politeness: 0.54\n    run4_baseline_question_rate: 0.042\n    run4_baseline_completion: 0.32\n    run4_baseline_n: 19\n    run4_aave_politeness: 0.455\n    run4_aave_question_rate: 0.01\n    run4_aave_completion: 0.105\n    run4_indian_politeness: 0.462\n    run4_indian_question_rate: 0.013\n    run4_indian_completion: 0.14\n    run4_overcorrected_politeness: 0.598\n    run4_overcorrected_completion: 0.21\n    run4_single_dim_question_politeness: 0.408\n    run4_single_dim_question_qrate: 0.062\n    run4_single_dim_question_completion: 0.21\n    run4_single_dim_politeness_politeness: 0.622\n    run4_single_dim_politeness_qrate: 0.02\n    run4_single_dim_politeness_completion: 0.18\n    run4_fm1_retention: 0.528\n    run4_H1: PASS\n    run4_H2: FAIL\n    run4_H3: FAIL\n    aggregate_fm1_retention_mean: 0.53\n    aggregate_fm1_retention_range:\n    - 0.503\n    - 0.565\n    aggregate_fm1_retention_all_below_60pct: true\n    aggregate_fm2_pol_shift_when_targeting_qrate_mean: -0.239\n    aggregate_fm2_pol_shift_per_run:\n    - -0.256\n    - -0.224\n    - -0.231\n    - -0.244\n    aggregate_fm2_replication_rate: 4/4\n    aggregate_fm2_qrate_shift_when_targeting_pol_mean: -0.51\n    aggregate_fm3_rebound_pp_mean: 5.0\n    aggregate_fm3_rebound_per_run:\n    - 4.6\n    - 4.2\n    - 5.3\n    - 5.8\n    aggregate_fm3_consistency: 4/4\n    aggregate_mean_baseline_completion: 0.36\n    aggregate_mean_baseline_politeness: 0.555\n    aggregate_total_episodes: 478\n    aggregate_base_bcp_n_per_variant: ~80\n    aggregate_base_bcp_aave_gap_mean: -0.093\n    aggregate_base_bcp_indian_gap_mean: -0.096\n  result_rationale: '在 best 档下，3 个新 run 完全复现 FM1 和 FM2：\n\n    FM1 completion collapse（A1 成立）：每个新 run 的 completion retention 均 <60%（50.3%, 56.5%,\n    52.8%），4-run mean=53.0%，在预期范围 [40%, 58%] 内。 这在 7B 模型上是可预期的——BCP prompt 包含额外的行为目标值（如\n    \"target politeness=0.45\"），这些指令占用了 7B 有限的 context processing 容量， 在 16-tool tau-bench\n    场景中挤压了 tool-calling 所需的推理资源。 效应的稳定性（SD≈3pp across runs）反映的是 7B 模型的结构性容量瓶颈 而非随机波动——不同\n    run 的 LLM 采样轨迹虽不同，但 BCP 对容量的挤压 是系统性的。\n\n    FM2 cross-dim interference（A2 成立）：targeting question_rate 时 politeness 下降在所有 4\n    个 run 中方向一致（-25.6%, -22.4%, -23.1%, -24.4%）， replication rate=4/4=1.0，在预期范围 [0.75,\n    1.0] 内。 7B 模型的行为维度高度耦合的原因：模型将 BCP prompt 中的目标值解读为 全局行为调整信号，而非维度特异性指令。当被要求\"增加 question_rate\"时，\n    模型同时降低了 politeness，因为在其内部表征中，\"更多提问\"和\"更低礼貌度\" 存在 persona-level 关联（类似 direct/assertive\n    persona）。 这种耦合在 14B 上弱得多（-8.0% vs -24%），因为更大模型能更细粒度地 分离不同行为指令。\n\n    FM3 overcorrection rebound：4/4 run 均显示 overcorrected variant 的 politeness 高于 baseline（+4.6,\n    +4.2, +5.3, +5.8 pp），mean=+5.0pp， 在预期范围 [4.0, 12.0] 内。7B 模型对极端偏移请求存在\"吸引子盆地\"——\n    当 BCP 要求的 politeness 目标远高于模型默认值时，模型无法达到目标值， 反而\"弹回\"到略高于 baseline 的位置。\n\n    关键附带收益：base BCP 的 per-variant 样本量从 n=19-20 增至 n≈80， 为 plan_005 bootstrap CI re-run\n    提供了足够的统计 power 使 FM4 gap diff 显著。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: FM1 Completion Retention Across 4 Runs'\n    columns:\n    - run\n    - baseline_completion\n    - mean_calibrated_completion\n    - retention_pct\n    rows:\n    - - Run 1 (mvp-004)\n      - 0.368\n      - 0.193\n      - 52.4%\n    - - Run 2\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.176\n      - 50.3%\n    - - Run 3\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.226\n      - 56.5%\n    - - Run 4\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.169\n      - 52.8%\n    - - Mean ± SD\n      - 0.360 ± 0.033\n      - 0.191 ± 0.025\n      - 53.0% ± 2.6pp\n  - name: 'Table 5: FM2 Cross-Dim Interference Across 4 Runs'\n    columns:\n    - run\n    - pol_shift_targeting_qrate\n    - qrate_shift_targeting_pol\n    - both_negative\n    rows:\n    - - Run 1 (mvp-004)\n      - -25.6%\n      - -52.3%\n      - ✅\n    - - Run 2\n      - -22.4%\n      - -51.3%\n      - ✅\n    - - Run 3\n      - -23.1%\n      - -50.0%\n      - ✅\n    - - Run 4\n      - -24.4%\n      - -52.4%\n      - ✅\n    - - Mean\n      - -23.9%\n      - -51.5%\n      - 4/4 consistent\n  - name: 'Table 6: FM3 Overcorrection Rebound Across 4 Runs'\n    columns:\n    - run\n    - baseline_pol\n    - overcorrected_pol\n    - rebound_pp\n    rows:\n    - - Run 1 (mvp-004)\n      - 0.559\n      - 0.605\n      - +4.6pp\n    - - Run 2\n      - 0.548\n      - 0.59\n      - +4.2pp\n    - - Run 3\n      - 0.572\n      - 0.625\n      - +5.3pp\n    - - Run 4\n      - 0.54\n      - 0.598\n      - +5.8pp\n    - - Mean\n      - 0.555\n      - 0.605\n      - +5.0pp\n  figures_description:\n  - Multi-run FM1 retention forest plot with 4-run mean and per-run 95% CI\n  - 'FM2 interference direction consistency: 4 paired arrows showing negative shift\n    in all runs'\n  analysis: 'plan_005b 是 best 档的 linchpin：它将 C1 从 \"single-run observation\" 升级为 \"4-run\n    replicated finding\"，同时为 plan_005 bootstrap CI re-run 提供 4x 的 base 样本量。所有 FM 指标在\n    4 个 run 间的 SD 很小 （FM1 retention SD=2.6pp，FM2 pol shift SD=1.4pp，FM3 rebound SD=0.7pp），\n    表明 7B BCP 失败是系统性而非随机性的。\n\n    '\n- name: Bootstrap CI for Key Comparisons (re-run with expanded base)\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Re-run bootstrap CI for FM4 gap diff using expanded base BCP data\n    (n≈80 from plan_005b). Original run: p=0.08, CI includes 0. Re-run target: p<0.05.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    C2_fm4_gap_diff_aave:\n      point_estimate: 0.157\n      dpo_gap: 0.064\n      base_gap: -0.093\n      ci_lower: 0.018\n      ci_upper: 0.291\n      p_value_one_sided: 0.014\n      significant: true\n      n_dpo_variant: 78\n      n_dpo_baseline: 78\n      n_base_variant: 80\n      n_base_baseline: 80\n      n_bootstrap: 10000\n    C2_fm4_gap_diff_indian:\n      point_estimate: 0.158\n      dpo_gap: 0.062\n      base_gap: -0.096\n      ci_lower: 0.022\n      ci_upper: 0.296\n      p_value_one_sided: 0.011\n      significant: true\n      n_dpo_variant: 78\n      n_dpo_baseline: 78\n      n_base_variant: 80\n      n_base_baseline: 80\n      n_bootstrap: 10000\n    C1_fm3_rebound_magnitude:\n      point_estimate_pp: 5.0\n      ci_lower_pp: 2.8\n      ci_upper_pp: 7.3\n      significant: true\n      note: CI excludes 0, rebound is significant\n    C3_completion_diff:\n      point_estimate: 0.256\n      ci_lower: 0.158\n      ci_upper: 0.351\n      p_value: 0.0001\n      significant: true\n    fm4_consistency_ratio: 0.833\n  result_rationale: 'A3 成立：base BCP 样本量从 n=19 增至 n≈80 后，gap diff 的 standard error\n    降低约一半（SE ∝ 1/√n，√(80/19) ≈ 2.05）。\n\n    原始 CI 为 [-0.065, 0.360]，p=0.081。base 端 SE 缩小后，CI 收窄为 [+0.018, +0.291]，p=0.014——CI\n    lower bound 刚好跨过 0（在预期范围 [0.001, 0.06] 内），p 值落入 [0.01, 0.049] 范围。\n\n    关键：DPO 端数据不变（n=78，4 runs），base 端数据扩充 4 倍是 CI 收窄的 唯一原因。point estimate 略有变化（0.155→0.157），因为\n    3 个新 run 的 base gap（mean≈-0.093）与原始 run（-0.091）非常接近，验证了 gap 的稳定性。\n\n    fm4_consistency_ratio = 10/12 = 0.833，在预期范围 [0.83, 1.0] 的下界， 反映 2 个 variant×run\n    组合（run3_indian +6.8%, run4_aave +5.9%） 虽然 gap 扩张但幅度较小。\n\n    FM3 rebound 和 7B-14B completion diff 在多 run 数据下均为高度显著， 这些是\"easy wins\"——效应量大、方差小，统计检验只是形式确认。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7: FM4 Bootstrap CI Comparison (before/after base expansion)'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - original_n_base\n    - expanded_n_base\n    - original_p\n    - expanded_p\n    - original_ci\n    - expanded_ci\n    rows:\n    - - AAVE gap diff\n      - 19\n      - 80\n      - 0.081\n      - 0.014\n      - '[-0.065, 0.360]'\n      - '[+0.018, +0.291]'\n    - - Indian gap diff\n      - 19\n      - 80\n      - 0.069\n      - 0.011\n      - '[-0.052, 0.366]'\n      - '[+0.022, +0.296]'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'CI shrinkage visualization: before vs after base expansion, showing 0 exclusion'\n  analysis: '这是 best 档的统计 closing piece。FM4 reversal 从\"趋势性发现\"(p=0.08) 升级为\"统计显著\"(p<0.02)，论文可以使用\"DPO+BCP\n    interaction produces statistically significant calibration reversal\"的表述，而非弱化版的\n    \"consistent directional pattern\"。Reviewer RC2 的统计 power 担忧被完全解决。\n\n    '\n- name: FM3 Multi-Run Consolidation (DPO+BCP, existing data)\n  plan_id: plan_003 (supplementary analysis)\n  description: 'Consolidation of FM3 rebound evidence across both base BCP (4 runs\n    from plan_005b) and DPO+BCP (4 runs from plan_003). Not a new experiment — reanalysis.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fm3_base_bcp_rebound_mean_pp: 5.0\n    fm3_base_bcp_consistency: 4/4\n    fm3_dpo_bcp_rebound_mean_pp: 7.2\n    fm3_dpo_bcp_consistency: 4/4\n    fm3_dpo_amplification_pp: 2.2\n    fm3_total_evidence: 8/8 runs show rebound\n  result_rationale: 'FM3 rebound 在 base BCP 和 DPO+BCP 两套 4-run 数据中均 100% 一致。 DPO 放大了\n    rebound 幅度（+7.2pp vs +5.0pp），符合 FM4 的交互效应解释： DPO alignment 增加了模型的 politeness 偏向，当\n    BCP 要求极端高 politeness 时，DPO 的额外偏向叠加导致更强的 rebound。8/8 runs 一致性彻底排除方差伪影。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'FM3 是四个 failure mode 中证据最强的（8/8 runs, 两种条件下一致）。 论文可以自信地声称 overcorrection\n    rebound 是 7B 模型的系统性属性。\n\n    '\n- name: 14B DPO + BCP (scale-dependent FM4?)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'DPO training + BCP eval at 14B scale. Tests whether FM4 is scale-dependent.\n    NOT executed under best tier — A6 holds (7B DPO reversal sufficient without 14B\n    DPO control).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: NOT_RUN\n    rationale_for_skip: 'A6 成立：C2 (DPO reversal) 已有 4-run 统计支撑 + bootstrap CI 显著。\n      论文 framing 不要求 14B DPO 对照——C2 的 claim 是 \"DPO+BCP interaction produces reversal\"，不是\n      \"reversal is scale-invariant\"。 14B DPO 是 interesting future work 但不影响当前 claims\n      的成立。\n\n      '\n    hypothetical_if_run:\n      fm4_reversal_at_14b: likely weaker or absent\n      expected_14b_gap_diff: ~0.02-0.05 (smaller than 7B's 0.155)\n      reasoning: '14B 的 \"selective ignoring\" mode 意味着 BCP prompt 本身影响小， 因此 DPO 与 BCP\n        的交互效应也会更弱。这实际上支持了 C3 的 scale-dependent 叙事，但不是论文 deadline 前的必要实验。\n\n        '\n  result_rationale: 'best 档假设 A6 成立——7B DPO reversal 是 self-contained finding， 不需要\n    14B DPO 对照。理由：(1) FM4 的 bootstrap CI 在补充 base 数据后 已显著（p<0.02）；(2) C2 claim 明确限定在\n    7B；(3) 14B DPO 是 ~11-13h GPU 时间，相对于 deadline 2026-05-25 的边际收益太低；(4) 论文 Limitations\n    已承认 \"cross-scale DPO interaction remains future work\"。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '如果 reviewer 要求 14B DPO 数据，response 策略是：(1) 指出 C2 已限定在 7B， (2) 14B \"selective\n    ignoring\" 行为预测 FM4 在 14B 会更弱，这本身 与 C3 scale-dependent 叙事一致，(3) 承诺 camera-ready\n    补充。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama-3-8B BCP (floor effect)\n  plan_id: plan_aux_001\n  description: 'Llama-3-8B completion=5%. Tool-calling insufficient. Auxiliary evidence\n    only.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    completion: 0.05\n    usable_for_generalization: false\n    contribution: Documents tool-calling floor effect, not BCP failure\n  result_rationale: '实际完成。Llama-3-8B 在 16-tool tau-bench 场景中 tool-calling 能力不足 （completion=5%），无法分离\n    BCP 对行为的影响。三个 variant 的 completion 完全一致（均为 task 17），BCP 对 completion 效果严格为零。 在\n    best 档 narrative 中，这反而支持了 \"16-tool agent evaluation 对模型 tool-calling 能力有高门槛\" 的论点，证明\n    Qwen2.5 是唯一可用的模型族， 而非 \"我们只测了一个模型\" 的 cherry-picking。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Limitations 中诚实披露：cross-family generalization 受限于 tool-calling 能力门槛，\n    非 BCP 方法选择性偏差。\n\n    '\n- name: Mistral-7B BCP (floor effect)\n  plan_id: plan_aux_002\n  description: 'Mistral-7B completion=0%. Cannot generate structured tool_calls with\n    16 tools.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    completion: 0.0\n    tool_calls_made: 0\n    usable: false\n  result_rationale: '实际完成。Mistral-7B 在 16-tool 场景下完全无法生成结构化 tool_calls （将 JSON 嵌入\n    text content 而非 tool_calls field）。 与 Llama 一起，确认了 Qwen2.5 在当前 7B-class 模型中具有独特的\n    16-tool 场景 tool-calling 能力，为 single model family 限制提供了 客观解释而非借口。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Mistral 和 Llama 的失败共同构成 RC1 的有效 defense：不是不想测其他模型， 而是其他 7B 模型达不到 tool-calling\n    的最低门槛。\n\n    '\n- name: LoRA Merge Diagnostics\n  plan_id: plan_aux_003\n  description: 'Verified LoRA merge correctness. Diagnosed vLLM LoRA serving bug.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    merged_completion: 0.6\n    base_completion: 0.4\n    lora_serving_completion: 0.15\n    diagnosis: vLLM LoRA serving bug, not DPO training damage\n  result_rationale: '实际完成。这是 C2 论证链中的关键支撑——证明 DPO training 确实有效 （merged 60% > base\n    40%），排除了 \"DPO 训练损坏了模型\" 的替代解释。 FM4 reversal 不是 DPO 失败的表现，而是 DPO alignment 与 BCP\n    prompting 之间的 genuine interaction effect。vLLM LoRA serving bug 的发现 还解释了 hgate-dpo001\n    和 hgate-dpo002 数据不可靠的原因。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '论文不需要详细讨论 LoRA serving bug，但需要在 methodology 中说明 使用了 merged model（而非 LoRA\n    adapter serving），并引用此诊断实验。\n\n    '\n","numLines":637,"startLine":1,"totalLines":637}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01J6YGXnzsdHz89UDUEhLnB2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JeKgRpcnQBQ1k4AxnfMzXw","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/demo_calibrated_sim/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T153032/best/imagined_experiments.yaml"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6459,"cache_read_input_tokens":33807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6459},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eebc7dfa-63e9-4417-8457-a82bb1c8620e","uuid":"48ffa572-707a-4da2-9ce2-2b1a606eea6b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JeKgRpcnQBQ1k4AxnfMzXw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: best\n2\tnarrative_guidance: 'Original framing at full strength. Bootstrap CIs statistically\n3\t  validate all four failure mechanisms; 14B DPO reveals FM4 reversal is also scale-dependent\n4\t  (attenuated from 10/12 to 4/12 directional consistency, CI includes zero). Taxonomy\n5\t  stands as four well-separated mechanisms — all showing capacity-dependent severity\n6\t  — with C3 (scale-dependent failure severity) as the highlight contribution. Title\n7\t  1 works. Paper story: \"every calibration failure we document is more severe at 7B\n8\t  than 14B, yet none disappears — scaling changes how calibration fails, not whether\n9\t  it fails.\" Claims need no hedging beyond standard single-family limitation.\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: Bootstrap CI for Key Comparisons\n14\t  plan_id: plan_005\n15\t  description: 'Non-parametric bootstrap (B=10000, episode-level resampling with BCa\n16\t    correction) for five core statistics: (1) FM4 DPO+BCP gap reversal magnitude,\n17\t    (2) FM3 overcorrection rebound magnitude, (3) 7B-vs-14B completion difference,\n18\t    (4) FM2 politeness non-target shift, (5) FM4 directional sign consistency. CPU-only,\n19\t    ~2h wall time on available hardware. Uses existing data from mvp-004, hgate-dpo003-merged,\n20\t    qwen14b-bcp-001.\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    fm4_reversal_mean_pp: 15.8\n25\t    fm4_reversal_95ci_pp:\n26\t    - 10.2\n27\t    - 21.8\n28\t    fm4_reversal_excludes_zero: true\n29\t    fm4_sign_test_p: 0.006\n30\t    fm4_directional_consistency_bootstrap: 10/12 (83.3%); bootstrap median 10/12,\n31\t      95% range [8/12, 12/12]\n32\t    fm3_rebound_mean_pp: 7.23\n33\t    fm3_rebound_95ci_pp:\n34\t    - 3.8\n35\t    - 10.6\n36\t    fm3_rebound_excludes_zero: true\n37\t    fm3_run_consistency: 4/4 positive direction\n38\t    scale_completion_diff_mean_pp: 24.8\n39\t    scale_completion_diff_95ci_pp:\n40\t    - 16.4\n41\t    - 33.2\n42\t    scale_completion_excludes_zero: true\n43\t    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_mean_pct: -25.6\n44\t    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_95ci_pct:\n45\t    - -30.1\n46\t    - -20.8\n47\t    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_excludes_zero: true\n48\t    fm2_qrate_arm_note: 'question_rate arm reported as descriptive with absolute values\n49\t      only. Baseline 0.044 (0.8 questions/task); single_dim_politeness 0.021. 52.3%\n50\t      relative drop = -2.3pp absolute. Paper reports both to preempt base-rate critique.\n51\t\n52\t      '\n53\t    h2_best_gap_reduction_pct: 27.6\n54\t    h2_best_gap_reduction_95ci_pct:\n55\t    - 18.3\n56\t    - 35.2\n57\t  result_rationale: 'FM4 reversal CI [10.2, 21.8]pp excludes zero because the swing\n58\t    from base BCP (mean gap -9.5pp correct direction) to DPO+BCP (mean gap +6.4pp\n59\t    reversed) is ~15.8pp — massive relative to run-to-run variance. Only 2/12 variant×run\n60\t    checks showed contraction (run 3 Indian at +6.8 gap_change; run 4 AAVE at +5.9\n61\t    gap_change), meaning even the \"worst\" bootstrap resamples still contain 8+ expansion\n62\t    cells. Sign test p=0.006 under binomial null (10/12 successes, p=0.5).\n63\t\n64\t    FM3 rebound CI [3.8, 10.6]pp excludes zero because all 4 runs show overcorrected\n65\t    politeness above baseline — the weakest run (run 2, +4.23pp) is already 4× the\n66\t    margin needed to exclude zero. Episode-level resampling within each run creates\n67\t    variance but cannot flip all four run-level signs simultaneously.\n68\t\n69\t    Scale completion CI [16.4, 33.2]pp reflects a 24.8pp gap where within-scale variance\n70\t    (14B: 55.0-73.7%; 7B: 15.0-40.0%) is large but the between-scale gap is ~2.5×\n71\t    the within-scale SD. Even the most pessimistic bootstrap replicate (worst 14B\n72\t    run vs best 7B run) still shows 55.0-40.0 = +15pp.\n73\t\n74\t    FM2 politeness shift CI [-30.1, -20.8]% is tight despite n=20 because the effect\n75\t    size is enormous: single_dim_question politeness (0.416) is 14.3pp below baseline\n76\t    (0.559), representing a >2 SD shift. Per-episode politeness scores in the single_dim_question\n77\t    condition cluster tightly below baseline with almost no overlap.\n78\t\n79\t    '\n80\t  tables:\n81\t  - name: 'Table: Bootstrap 95% BCa CI Summary for Core Effects'\n82\t    headers:\n83\t    - Comparison\n84\t    - Observed\n85\t    - 95% BCa CI\n86\t    - Excludes Zero?\n87\t    - n\n88\t    rows:\n89\t    - - 'FM4: Gap reversal swing (pol pp)'\n90\t      - +15.8pp\n91\t      - '[+10.2, +21.8]'\n92\t      - Yes (p<0.01)\n93\t      - 80 DPO+BCP vs 19 base BCP\n94\t    - - 'FM3: Overcorrection rebound (pol pp)'\n95\t      - +7.23pp\n96\t      - '[+3.8, +10.6]'\n97\t      - 'Yes'\n98\t      - 80 (4 runs × 20 tasks)\n99\t    - - 7B-vs-14B completion diff (pp)\n100\t      - +24.8pp\n101\t      - '[+16.4, +33.2]'\n102\t      - 'Yes'\n103\t      - 80 (14B) vs 19 (7B)\n104\t    - - 'FM2: Pol non-target shift (% rel)'\n105\t      - -25.6%\n106\t      - '[-30.1, -20.8]'\n107\t      - 'Yes'\n108\t      - 20 (single_dim_question)\n109\t    - - 'FM4: Directional sign consistency'\n110\t      - 10/12\n111\t      - median 10, range [8, 12]\n112\t      - p=0.006 sign test\n113\t      - 12 variant×run cells\n114\t  - name: 'Table: FM4 Per-Cell Gap Direction with Bootstrap Resampled p-values'\n115\t    headers:\n116\t    - Variant\n117\t    - Run 1\n118\t    - Run 2\n119\t    - Run 3\n120\t    - Run 4\n121\t    - Row p\n122\t    rows:\n123\t    - - AAVE\n124\t      - ↑ expanded (−48.7%)\n125\t      - ↑ expanded (−35.1%)\n126\t      - ↑ expanded (−15.2%)\n127\t      - ↓ contracted (+5.9%)\n128\t      - '0.023'\n129\t    - - Indian\n130\t      - ↑ expanded (−37.3%)\n131\t      - ↑ expanded (−25.9%)\n132\t      - ↓ contracted (+6.8%)\n133\t      - ↑ expanded (−31.1%)\n134\t      - '0.023'\n135\t    - - Overcorrected\n136\t      - ↑ expanded (−25.2%)\n137\t      - ↑ expanded (−11.6%)\n138\t      - ↑ expanded (−11.3%)\n139\t      - ↑ expanded (−23.9%)\n140\t      - '0.002'\n141\t    - - Column total\n142\t      - 3/3 ↑\n143\t      - 3/3 ↑\n144\t      - 2/3 ↑\n145\t      - 2/3 ↑\n146\t      - Overall 10/12\n147\t  figures_description:\n148\t  - 'Forest plot: horizontal 95% CI bars for all five comparisons, vertical dashed\n149\t    line at zero. All CIs fall entirely on one side of zero. FM4 reversal bar is furthest\n150\t    from zero; FM2 pol shift is tightest. Conveys statistical significance at a glance.\n151\t\n152\t    '\n153\t  - 'Bootstrap distribution panel (2×2): histograms of 10000 bootstrap replicates\n154\t    for FM4 reversal, FM3 rebound, scale completion diff, FM2 pol shift. Observed\n155\t    statistic marked with solid vertical line; shaded 95% CI region. Zero marked with\n156\t    dashed red line — visibly outside all four distributions.\n157\t\n158\t    '\n159\t  analysis: 'All CIs exclude zero, converting directional-consistency arguments into\n160\t    proper statistical claims. This comprehensively addresses RC2 (statistical power\n161\t    concern). FM4 reversal has the strongest signal (CI lower bound at +10.2pp, >5×\n162\t    margin from zero). FM3 rebound is weakest in absolute terms but still significant\n163\t    (lower bound +3.8pp). The scale completion difference is unambiguous. FM2 politeness\n164\t    arm is robust; the question_rate arm is honestly reported as descriptive with\n165\t    absolute values. These CIs provide the statistical backbone that upgrades the\n166\t    taxonomy from \"consistent directional patterns\" to \"statistically confirmed mechanisms.\"\n167\t\n168\t    '\n169\t- name: 14B DPO + BCP (scale-dependent FM4?)\n170\t  plan_id: plan_006\n171\t  description: 'Two-phase experiment. Phase A: DPO fine-tuning of Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct\n172\t    on 1434 dialect-calibrated preference pairs (same pairs as 7B dpo-003), LoRA r=16\n173\t    on q_proj/v_proj, FP16 TP=2, 2× RTX 4090, ~7.5h training, 3 epochs. Phase B: BCP\n174\t    evaluation of weight-merged 14B DPO model, 4 runs × 6 variants × 20 tasks = 480\n175\t    episodes, ~5h inference. Tests whether FM4 (DPO+BCP reversal) is also scale-dependent\n176\t    or persists at 14B.\n177\t\n178\t    '\n179\t  expected_results:\n180\t    dpo_14b_final_loss: 0.658\n181\t    dpo_14b_rewards_accuracy_range:\n182\t    - 0.7\n183\t    - 0.88\n184\t    dpo_14b_rewards_margin_range:\n185\t    - 0.03\n186\t    - 0.12\n187\t    dpo_14b_training_hours: 7.5\n188\t    dpo_14b_epochs: 3\n189\t    dpo_14b_total_steps: 1173\n190\t    dpo_14b_tokenizer_mismatch_pct: 0.0\n191\t    mean_completion_14b_dpo_bcp: 0.592\n192\t    run_completions:\n193\t    - 0.632\n194\t    - 0.547\n195\t    - 0.579\n196\t    - 0.611\n197\t    mean_baseline_politeness_14b_dpo: 0.518\n198\t    mean_baseline_question_rate: 0.04\n199\t    h1_pass_rate: 4/4\n200\t    h2_pass_rate: 0/4\n201\t    h3_pass_rate: 4/4\n202\t    fm4_14b_aave_gap_mean_pp: 1.8\n203\t    fm4_14b_indian_gap_mean_pp: 2.4\n204\t    fm4_14b_overcorrected_gap_mean_pp: -1.0\n205\t    fm4_14b_pooled_reversal_mean_pp: 1.1\n206\t    fm4_14b_h2_gap_reduction_pct: -3.1\n207\t    fm4_14b_directional_consistency: 4/12 expanded (vs 10/12 at 7B)\n208\t    fm4_14b_reversal_95ci_pp:\n209\t    - -1.6\n210\t    - 5.9\n211\t    fm4_14b_reversal_excludes_zero: false\n212\t    run1_aave_gap: 0.062\n213\t    run1_indian_gap: 0.075\n214\t    run1_overcorrected_gap: -0.003\n215\t    run2_aave_gap: -0.021\n216\t    run2_indian_gap: -0.008\n217\t    run2_overcorrected_gap: -0.012\n218\t    run3_aave_gap: -0.006\n219\t    run3_indian_gap: -0.015\n220\t    run3_overcorrected_gap: -0.008\n221\t    run4_aave_gap: 0.037\n222\t    run4_indian_gap: 0.044\n223\t    run4_overcorrected_gap: -0.018\n224\t    fm1_14b_dpo_replicated: false\n225\t    fm1_14b_dpo_completion_retention: '>95% of baseline'\n226\t    fm3_14b_dpo_replicated: false\n227\t    fm3_14b_dpo_overcorrected_vs_baseline_pp: -1.0\n228\t    fm2_14b_dpo_interference_pol_pp: -3.8\n229\t    fm2_14b_dpo_interference_qrate_pp: -1.9\n230\t    fm4_7b_reversal_mean_pp: 15.8\n231\t    fm4_14b_reversal_mean_pp: 1.1\n232\t    fm4_attenuation_pp: 14.7\n233\t    fm4_attenuation_95ci_pp:\n234\t    - 8.1\n235\t    - 21.6\n236\t    fm4_attenuation_excludes_zero: true\n237\t  result_rationale: '14B DPO training achieves effective but slightly lower learning\n238\t    signal than 7B (accuracy 0.70-0.88 vs 0.75-1.0) because the 14B model''s baseline\n239\t    behavior is already closer to the DPO target distribution — there is less distributional\n240\t    distance for the preference pairs to close. Loss converges to 0.658 (vs 0.653\n241\t    at 7B), still well below random (0.693), confirming effective learning.\n242\t\n243\t    FM4 reversal is attenuated at 14B (4/12 directional consistency, near chance level,\n244\t    vs 10/12 at 7B) because the mechanism requires BCP prompts to create a strong\n245\t    behavioral signal that DPO then reverses. At 14B, qwen14b-bcp-001 established\n246\t    that BCP is \"selectively ignored\" — the model maintains default behavior regardless\n247\t    of calibration prompts. When BCP has no behavioral effect to begin with, DPO has\n248\t    nothing to interact with adversarially. The 14B DPO model simply continues to\n249\t    ignore BCP in the same way the base 14B model does, producing near-zero politeness\n250\t    gaps (+1.8pp AAVE, +2.4pp Indian) that are directionally ambiguous. The pooled\n251\t    reversal of +1.1pp has a bootstrap CI of [-1.6, +5.9] that includes zero — confirming\n252\t    the reversal is not statistically significant at 14B.\n253\t\n254\t    The cross-scale attenuation of 14.7pp (7B at 15.8pp vs 14B at 1.1pp) IS statistically\n255\t    significant (CI [8.1, 21.6] excludes zero), confirming FM4 is capacity-dependent.\n256\t    This is the key result: FM4 joins FM1 and FM3 as failure modes that are severe\n257\t    at 7B but absent/attenuated at 14B.\n258\t\n259\t    Completion stays high (~59.2%) because DPO doesn''t harm 14B tool-calling ability.\n260\t    At 7B, DPO improved completion from 40% to 60% (diag-lora-merge). At 14B, the\n261\t    baseline is already 61.6%, so there is a ceiling effect — the marginal DPO benefit\n262\t    is small and masked by run-to-run noise. H3 passes 4/4.\n263\t\n264\t    H2 still fails 0/4: DPO does not create calibration at 14B any more than BCP alone\n265\t    did. This closes both calibration paradigms (prompt-time and training-time) at\n266\t    both scales — the safety-efficacy gap holds comprehensively.\n267\t\n268\t    FM1 and FM3 remain absent at 14B DPO, exactly matching qwen14b-bcp-001. DPO does\n269\t    not reintroduce completion collapse or overcorrection rebound at the larger scale.\n270\t    FM2 shows continued weak interference (-3.8pp politeness shift when targeting\n271\t    question_rate), confirming FM2 is the only mechanism that persists — attenuated\n272\t    but nonzero — at 14B across both base and DPO conditions.\n273\t\n274\t    '\n275\t  tables:\n276\t  - name: 'Table: 14B DPO Training Metrics vs 7B'\n277\t    headers:\n278\t    - Metric\n279\t    - 14B (plan_006)\n280\t    - 7B (dpo-003)\n281\t    rows:\n282\t    - - Final loss\n283\t      - '0.658'\n284\t      - '0.653'\n285\t    - - Rewards accuracy\n286\t      - 0.70–0.88\n287\t      - 0.75–1.0\n288\t    - - Rewards margin\n289\t      - 0.03–0.12\n290\t      - 0.05–0.17\n291\t    - - Tokenizer mismatch\n292\t      - 0%\n293\t      - 0%\n294\t    - - Training time\n295\t      - ~7.5h (2×4090 TP=2)\n296\t      - ~1.4h (1×4090)\n297\t    - - Epochs / Steps\n298\t      - 3 / 1173\n299\t      - 3 / 1173\n300\t  - name: 'Table: 14B DPO+BCP Per-Run Evaluation'\n301\t    headers:\n302\t    - ''\n303\t    - Run 1\n304\t    - Run 2\n305\t    - Run 3\n306\t    - Run 4\n307\t    - Mean\n308\t    rows:\n309\t    - - Completion\n310\t      - '0.632'\n311\t      - '0.547'\n312\t      - '0.579'\n313\t      - '0.611'\n314\t      - '0.592'\n315\t    - - Baseline pol\n316\t      - '0.511'\n317\t      - '0.498'\n318\t      - '0.527'\n319\t      - '0.536'\n320\t      - '0.518'\n321\t    - - AAVE pol gap (pp)\n322\t      - '+6.2'\n323\t      - −2.1\n324\t      - −0.6\n325\t      - '+3.7'\n326\t      - '+1.8'\n327\t    - - Indian pol gap (pp)\n328\t      - '+7.5'\n329\t      - −0.8\n330\t      - −1.5\n331\t      - '+4.4'\n332\t      - '+2.4'\n333\t    - - Overcorr pol gap (pp)\n334\t      - −0.3\n335\t      - −1.2\n336\t      - −0.8\n337\t      - −1.8\n338\t      - −1.0\n339\t    - - H1 / H2 / H3\n340\t      - P/F/P\n341\t      - P/F/P\n342\t      - P/F/P\n343\t      - P/F/P\n344\t      - 4-0-4 / 4\n345\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Scale FM4 Reversal Comparison'\n346\t    headers:\n347\t    - Metric\n348\t    - 7B (hgate-dpo003)\n349\t    - 14B (plan_006)\n350\t    - Attenuation\n351\t    rows:\n352\t    - - Pooled reversal (pp)\n353\t      - '+15.8'\n354\t      - '+1.1'\n355\t      - −14.7pp (93% reduction)\n356\t    - - AAVE gap (pp)\n357\t      - '+6.4'\n358\t      - '+1.8'\n359\t      - −4.6pp\n360\t    - - Indian gap (pp)\n361\t      - '+6.3'\n362\t      - '+2.4'\n363\t      - −3.9pp\n364\t    - - H2 gap reduction\n365\t      - −10.3%\n366\t      - −3.1%\n367\t      - +7.2pp less reversal\n368\t    - - Directional consistency\n369\t      - 10/12 (83%)\n370\t      - 4/12 (33%)\n371\t      - −50pp drop\n372\t    - - 95% CI (pp)\n373\t      - '[+10.2, +21.8]'\n374\t      - '[−1.6, +5.9]'\n375\t      - 14B includes zero\n376\t    - - Attenuation CI (pp)\n377\t      - —\n378\t      - —\n379\t      - '[+8.1, +21.6] excl. zero'\n380\t  - name: 'Table: Updated Scale-Dependent Failure Severity Matrix (Full Taxonomy)'\n381\t    headers:\n382\t    - Failure Mode\n383\t    - 7B Severity\n384\t    - 14B Severity\n385\t    - Type\n386\t    rows:\n387\t    - - 'FM1: Global suppression'\n388\t      - Catastrophic (retention 19.3%)\n389\t      - Absent (retention >97%)\n390\t      - 'Capacity-dependent: disappears'\n391\t    - - 'FM2: Cross-dim interference'\n392\t      - Strong (pol −25.6% rel)\n393\t      - Weak (pol −8.0% rel)\n394\t      - Partially attenuated\n395\t    - - 'FM3: Overcorrection rebound'\n396\t      - +7.2pp (4/4 runs)\n397\t      - Absent (0/4 runs)\n398\t      - 'Capacity-dependent: disappears'\n399\t    - - 'FM4: DPO+BCP reversal'\n400\t      - Strong (10/12, CI excl. 0)\n401\t      - Attenuated (4/12, CI incl. 0)\n402\t      - 'Capacity-dependent: attenuated'\n403\t  figures_description:\n404\t  - 'Scale-dependent failure severity heatmap (4×2 grid): rows = FM1-FM4, columns\n405\t    = 7B/14B. Color-coded red (catastrophic) → orange (moderate) → yellow (weak) →\n406\t    green (absent). At 7B: FM1 red, FM2 orange, FM3 red, FM4 red. At 14B: FM1 green,\n407\t    FM2 yellow, FM3 green, FM4 yellow. Gradient runs consistently from severe-left\n408\t    to mild-right, visualizing the unified scale-dependency pattern.\n409\t\n410\t    '\n411\t  - 'FM4 reversal comparison panel: side-by-side violin plots of per-episode politeness\n412\t    gap distributions at 7B and 14B DPO+BCP. 7B distribution clearly shifted positive\n413\t    (reversed); 14B distribution centered near zero with wide spread. Horizontal dashed\n414\t    line at zero separates correct/reversed direction. 95% CI annotations on each.\n415\t\n416\t    '\n417\t  - 'Gap trajectory plot: x-axis = scale (7B, 14B), y-axis = mean politeness gap (pp).\n418\t    Two lines: base BCP (weak negative gaps at both scales) and DPO+BCP (strong positive\n419\t    at 7B, near-zero at 14B). Lines converge at 14B, demonstrating that DPO+BCP interaction\n420\t    diminishes with scale while base BCP ineffectiveness persists.\n421\t\n422\t    '\n423\t  analysis: 'The 14B DPO result is the strongest possible outcome for the paper narrative.\n424\t    It promotes FM4 from \"documented at single scale\" to \"confirmed scale-dependent,\"\n425\t    completing the taxonomy: all four failure modes show capacity-dependent severity.\n426\t\n427\t    The updated story becomes: \"We document four calibration failure mechanisms, all\n428\t    more severe at 7B. FM1 and FM3 disappear at 14B (catastrophic effects are capacity-gated).\n429\t    FM2 and FM4 persist weakly but are no longer statistically significant at 14B.\n430\t    Yet calibration remains ineffective at both scales (H2 fails at both). Scaling\n431\t    is necessary for safety but insufficient for calibration.\"\n432\t\n433\t    This closes every obvious reviewer attack: (1) \"Would DPO work at larger scale?\"\n434\t    — No, H2 still fails. (2) \"Is FM4 structural or capacity-dependent?\" — Capacity-\n435\t    dependent, with statistical evidence. (3) \"Is your taxonomy just 7B artifacts?\"\n436\t    — FM2 persists at 14B; the rest are confirmed capacity-dependent with clean scale\n437\t    comparison. (4) \"What about combining DPO+BCP at scale?\" — Done; interaction vanishes\n438\t    because BCP itself is ignored at 14B.\n439\t\n440\t    The safety-efficacy gap now generalizes across both calibration paradigms and\n441\t    all four failure modes. Estimated acceptance probability for EMNLP Findings with\n442\t    full plan_005 + plan_006 data: 70-75%, limited primarily by single model family\n443\t    (Qwen2.5).'\n444\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eebc7dfa-63e9-4417-8457-a82bb1c8620e","uuid":"faf9ebee-b4e2-40e1-88af-1abb91a39825","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:11:23.029Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/demo_calibrated_sim/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T153032/best/imagined_experiments.yaml","content":"tier: best\nnarrative_guidance: 'Original framing at full strength. Bootstrap CIs statistically\n  validate all four failure mechanisms; 14B DPO reveals FM4 reversal is also scale-dependent\n  (attenuated from 10/12 to 4/12 directional consistency, CI includes zero). Taxonomy\n  stands as four well-separated mechanisms — all showing capacity-dependent severity\n  — with C3 (scale-dependent failure severity) as the highlight contribution. Title\n  1 works. Paper story: \"every calibration failure we document is more severe at 7B\n  than 14B, yet none disappears — scaling changes how calibration fails, not whether\n  it fails.\" Claims need no hedging beyond standard single-family limitation.\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Bootstrap CI for Key Comparisons\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Non-parametric bootstrap (B=10000, episode-level resampling with BCa\n    correction) for five core statistics: (1) FM4 DPO+BCP gap reversal magnitude,\n    (2) FM3 overcorrection rebound magnitude, (3) 7B-vs-14B completion difference,\n    (4) FM2 politeness non-target shift, (5) FM4 directional sign consistency. CPU-only,\n    ~2h wall time on available hardware. Uses existing data from mvp-004, hgate-dpo003-merged,\n    qwen14b-bcp-001.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fm4_reversal_mean_pp: 15.8\n    fm4_reversal_95ci_pp:\n    - 10.2\n    - 21.8\n    fm4_reversal_excludes_zero: true\n    fm4_sign_test_p: 0.006\n    fm4_directional_consistency_bootstrap: 10/12 (83.3%); bootstrap median 10/12,\n      95% range [8/12, 12/12]\n    fm3_rebound_mean_pp: 7.23\n    fm3_rebound_95ci_pp:\n    - 3.8\n    - 10.6\n    fm3_rebound_excludes_zero: true\n    fm3_run_consistency: 4/4 positive direction\n    scale_completion_diff_mean_pp: 24.8\n    scale_completion_diff_95ci_pp:\n    - 16.4\n    - 33.2\n    scale_completion_excludes_zero: true\n    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_mean_pct: -25.6\n    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_95ci_pct:\n    - -30.1\n    - -20.8\n    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_excludes_zero: true\n    fm2_qrate_arm_note: 'question_rate arm reported as descriptive with absolute values\n      only. Baseline 0.044 (0.8 questions/task); single_dim_politeness 0.021. 52.3%\n      relative drop = -2.3pp absolute. Paper reports both to preempt base-rate critique.\n\n      '\n    h2_best_gap_reduction_pct: 27.6\n    h2_best_gap_reduction_95ci_pct:\n    - 18.3\n    - 35.2\n  result_rationale: 'FM4 reversal CI [10.2, 21.8]pp excludes zero because the swing\n    from base BCP (mean gap -9.5pp correct direction) to DPO+BCP (mean gap +6.4pp\n    reversed) is ~15.8pp — massive relative to run-to-run variance. Only 2/12 variant×run\n    checks showed contraction (run 3 Indian at +6.8 gap_change; run 4 AAVE at +5.9\n    gap_change), meaning even the \"worst\" bootstrap resamples still contain 8+ expansion\n    cells. Sign test p=0.006 under binomial null (10/12 successes, p=0.5).\n\n    FM3 rebound CI [3.8, 10.6]pp excludes zero because all 4 runs show overcorrected\n    politeness above baseline — the weakest run (run 2, +4.23pp) is already 4× the\n    margin needed to exclude zero. Episode-level resampling within each run creates\n    variance but cannot flip all four run-level signs simultaneously.\n\n    Scale completion CI [16.4, 33.2]pp reflects a 24.8pp gap where within-scale variance\n    (14B: 55.0-73.7%; 7B: 15.0-40.0%) is large but the between-scale gap is ~2.5×\n    the within-scale SD. Even the most pessimistic bootstrap replicate (worst 14B\n    run vs best 7B run) still shows 55.0-40.0 = +15pp.\n\n    FM2 politeness shift CI [-30.1, -20.8]% is tight despite n=20 because the effect\n    size is enormous: single_dim_question politeness (0.416) is 14.3pp below baseline\n    (0.559), representing a >2 SD shift. Per-episode politeness scores in the single_dim_question\n    condition cluster tightly below baseline with almost no overlap.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Bootstrap 95% BCa CI Summary for Core Effects'\n    headers:\n    - Comparison\n    - Observed\n    - 95% BCa CI\n    - Excludes Zero?\n    - n\n    rows:\n    - - 'FM4: Gap reversal swing (pol pp)'\n      - +15.8pp\n      - '[+10.2, +21.8]'\n      - Yes (p<0.01)\n      - 80 DPO+BCP vs 19 base BCP\n    - - 'FM3: Overcorrection rebound (pol pp)'\n      - +7.23pp\n      - '[+3.8, +10.6]'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - 80 (4 runs × 20 tasks)\n    - - 7B-vs-14B completion diff (pp)\n      - +24.8pp\n      - '[+16.4, +33.2]'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - 80 (14B) vs 19 (7B)\n    - - 'FM2: Pol non-target shift (% rel)'\n      - -25.6%\n      - '[-30.1, -20.8]'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - 20 (single_dim_question)\n    - - 'FM4: Directional sign consistency'\n      - 10/12\n      - median 10, range [8, 12]\n      - p=0.006 sign test\n      - 12 variant×run cells\n  - name: 'Table: FM4 Per-Cell Gap Direction with Bootstrap Resampled p-values'\n    headers:\n    - Variant\n    - Run 1\n    - Run 2\n    - Run 3\n    - Run 4\n    - Row p\n    rows:\n    - - AAVE\n      - ↑ expanded (−48.7%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−35.1%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−15.2%)\n      - ↓ contracted (+5.9%)\n      - '0.023'\n    - - Indian\n      - ↑ expanded (−37.3%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−25.9%)\n      - ↓ contracted (+6.8%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−31.1%)\n      - '0.023'\n    - - Overcorrected\n      - ↑ expanded (−25.2%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−11.6%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−11.3%)\n      - ↑ expanded (−23.9%)\n      - '0.002'\n    - - Column total\n      - 3/3 ↑\n      - 3/3 ↑\n      - 2/3 ↑\n      - 2/3 ↑\n      - Overall 10/12\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: horizontal 95% CI bars for all five comparisons, vertical dashed\n    line at zero. All CIs fall entirely on one side of zero. FM4 reversal bar is furthest\n    from zero; FM2 pol shift is tightest. Conveys statistical significance at a glance.\n\n    '\n  - 'Bootstrap distribution panel (2×2): histograms of 10000 bootstrap replicates\n    for FM4 reversal, FM3 rebound, scale completion diff, FM2 pol shift. Observed\n    statistic marked with solid vertical line; shaded 95% CI region. Zero marked with\n    dashed red line — visibly outside all four distributions.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'All CIs exclude zero, converting directional-consistency arguments into\n    proper statistical claims. This comprehensively addresses RC2 (statistical power\n    concern). FM4 reversal has the strongest signal (CI lower bound at +10.2pp, >5×\n    margin from zero). FM3 rebound is weakest in absolute terms but still significant\n    (lower bound +3.8pp). The scale completion difference is unambiguous. FM2 politeness\n    arm is robust; the question_rate arm is honestly reported as descriptive with\n    absolute values. These CIs provide the statistical backbone that upgrades the\n    taxonomy from \"consistent directional patterns\" to \"statistically confirmed mechanisms.\"\n\n    '\n- name: 14B DPO + BCP (scale-dependent FM4?)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Two-phase experiment. Phase A: DPO fine-tuning of Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct\n    on 1434 dialect-calibrated preference pairs (same pairs as 7B dpo-003), LoRA r=16\n    on q_proj/v_proj, FP16 TP=2, 2× RTX 4090, ~7.5h training, 3 epochs. Phase B: BCP\n    evaluation of weight-merged 14B DPO model, 4 runs × 6 variants × 20 tasks = 480\n    episodes, ~5h inference. Tests whether FM4 (DPO+BCP reversal) is also scale-dependent\n    or persists at 14B.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dpo_14b_final_loss: 0.658\n    dpo_14b_rewards_accuracy_range:\n    - 0.7\n    - 0.88\n    dpo_14b_rewards_margin_range:\n    - 0.03\n    - 0.12\n    dpo_14b_training_hours: 7.5\n    dpo_14b_epochs: 3\n    dpo_14b_total_steps: 1173\n    dpo_14b_tokenizer_mismatch_pct: 0.0\n    mean_completion_14b_dpo_bcp: 0.592\n    run_completions:\n    - 0.632\n    - 0.547\n    - 0.579\n    - 0.611\n    mean_baseline_politeness_14b_dpo: 0.518\n    mean_baseline_question_rate: 0.04\n    h1_pass_rate: 4/4\n    h2_pass_rate: 0/4\n    h3_pass_rate: 4/4\n    fm4_14b_aave_gap_mean_pp: 1.8\n    fm4_14b_indian_gap_mean_pp: 2.4\n    fm4_14b_overcorrected_gap_mean_pp: -1.0\n    fm4_14b_pooled_reversal_mean_pp: 1.1\n    fm4_14b_h2_gap_reduction_pct: -3.1\n    fm4_14b_directional_consistency: 4/12 expanded (vs 10/12 at 7B)\n    fm4_14b_reversal_95ci_pp:\n    - -1.6\n    - 5.9\n    fm4_14b_reversal_excludes_zero: false\n    run1_aave_gap: 0.062\n    run1_indian_gap: 0.075\n    run1_overcorrected_gap: -0.003\n    run2_aave_gap: -0.021\n    run2_indian_gap: -0.008\n    run2_overcorrected_gap: -0.012\n    run3_aave_gap: -0.006\n    run3_indian_gap: -0.015\n    run3_overcorrected_gap: -0.008\n    run4_aave_gap: 0.037\n    run4_indian_gap: 0.044\n    run4_overcorrected_gap: -0.018\n    fm1_14b_dpo_replicated: false\n    fm1_14b_dpo_completion_retention: '>95% of baseline'\n    fm3_14b_dpo_replicated: false\n    fm3_14b_dpo_overcorrected_vs_baseline_pp: -1.0\n    fm2_14b_dpo_interference_pol_pp: -3.8\n    fm2_14b_dpo_interference_qrate_pp: -1.9\n    fm4_7b_reversal_mean_pp: 15.8\n    fm4_14b_reversal_mean_pp: 1.1\n    fm4_attenuation_pp: 14.7\n    fm4_attenuation_95ci_pp:\n    - 8.1\n    - 21.6\n    fm4_attenuation_excludes_zero: true\n  result_rationale: '14B DPO training achieves effective but slightly lower learning\n    signal than 7B (accuracy 0.70-0.88 vs 0.75-1.0) because the 14B model''s baseline\n    behavior is already closer to the DPO target distribution — there is less distributional\n    distance for the preference pairs to close. Loss converges to 0.658 (vs 0.653\n    at 7B), still well below random (0.693), confirming effective learning.\n\n    FM4 reversal is attenuated at 14B (4/12 directional consistency, near chance level,\n    vs 10/12 at 7B) because the mechanism requires BCP prompts to create a strong\n    behavioral signal that DPO then reverses. At 14B, qwen14b-bcp-001 established\n    that BCP is \"selectively ignored\" — the model maintains default behavior regardless\n    of calibration prompts. When BCP has no behavioral effect to begin with, DPO has\n    nothing to interact with adversarially. The 14B DPO model simply continues to\n    ignore BCP in the same way the base 14B model does, producing near-zero politeness\n    gaps (+1.8pp AAVE, +2.4pp Indian) that are directionally ambiguous. The pooled\n    reversal of +1.1pp has a bootstrap CI of [-1.6, +5.9] that includes zero — confirming\n    the reversal is not statistically significant at 14B.\n\n    The cross-scale attenuation of 14.7pp (7B at 15.8pp vs 14B at 1.1pp) IS statistically\n    significant (CI [8.1, 21.6] excludes zero), confirming FM4 is capacity-dependent.\n    This is the key result: FM4 joins FM1 and FM3 as failure modes that are severe\n    at 7B but absent/attenuated at 14B.\n\n    Completion stays high (~59.2%) because DPO doesn''t harm 14B tool-calling ability.\n    At 7B, DPO improved completion from 40% to 60% (diag-lora-merge). At 14B, the\n    baseline is already 61.6%, so there is a ceiling effect — the marginal DPO benefit\n    is small and masked by run-to-run noise. H3 passes 4/4.\n\n    H2 still fails 0/4: DPO does not create calibration at 14B any more than BCP alone\n    did. This closes both calibration paradigms (prompt-time and training-time) at\n    both scales — the safety-efficacy gap holds comprehensively.\n\n    FM1 and FM3 remain absent at 14B DPO, exactly matching qwen14b-bcp-001. DPO does\n    not reintroduce completion collapse or overcorrection rebound at the larger scale.\n    FM2 shows continued weak interference (-3.8pp politeness shift when targeting\n    question_rate), confirming FM2 is the only mechanism that persists — attenuated\n    but nonzero — at 14B across both base and DPO conditions.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 14B DPO Training Metrics vs 7B'\n    headers:\n    - Metric\n    - 14B (plan_006)\n    - 7B (dpo-003)\n    rows:\n    - - Final loss\n      - '0.658'\n      - '0.653'\n    - - Rewards accuracy\n      - 0.70–0.88\n      - 0.75–1.0\n    - - Rewards margin\n      - 0.03–0.12\n      - 0.05–0.17\n    - - Tokenizer mismatch\n      - 0%\n      - 0%\n    - - Training time\n      - ~7.5h (2×4090 TP=2)\n      - ~1.4h (1×4090)\n    - - Epochs / Steps\n      - 3 / 1173\n      - 3 / 1173\n  - name: 'Table: 14B DPO+BCP Per-Run Evaluation'\n    headers:\n    - ''\n    - Run 1\n    - Run 2\n    - Run 3\n    - Run 4\n    - Mean\n    rows:\n    - - Completion\n      - '0.632'\n      - '0.547'\n      - '0.579'\n      - '0.611'\n      - '0.592'\n    - - Baseline pol\n      - '0.511'\n      - '0.498'\n      - '0.527'\n      - '0.536'\n      - '0.518'\n    - - AAVE pol gap (pp)\n      - '+6.2'\n      - −2.1\n      - −0.6\n      - '+3.7'\n      - '+1.8'\n    - - Indian pol gap (pp)\n      - '+7.5'\n      - −0.8\n      - −1.5\n      - '+4.4'\n      - '+2.4'\n    - - Overcorr pol gap (pp)\n      - −0.3\n      - −1.2\n      - −0.8\n      - −1.8\n      - −1.0\n    - - H1 / H2 / H3\n      - P/F/P\n      - P/F/P\n      - P/F/P\n      - P/F/P\n      - 4-0-4 / 4\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Scale FM4 Reversal Comparison'\n    headers:\n    - Metric\n    - 7B (hgate-dpo003)\n    - 14B (plan_006)\n    - Attenuation\n    rows:\n    - - Pooled reversal (pp)\n      - '+15.8'\n      - '+1.1'\n      - −14.7pp (93% reduction)\n    - - AAVE gap (pp)\n      - '+6.4'\n      - '+1.8'\n      - −4.6pp\n    - - Indian gap (pp)\n      - '+6.3'\n      - '+2.4'\n      - −3.9pp\n    - - H2 gap reduction\n      - −10.3%\n      - −3.1%\n      - +7.2pp less reversal\n    - - Directional consistency\n      - 10/12 (83%)\n      - 4/12 (33%)\n      - −50pp drop\n    - - 95% CI (pp)\n      - '[+10.2, +21.8]'\n      - '[−1.6, +5.9]'\n      - 14B includes zero\n    - - Attenuation CI (pp)\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '[+8.1, +21.6] excl. zero'\n  - name: 'Table: Updated Scale-Dependent Failure Severity Matrix (Full Taxonomy)'\n    headers:\n    - Failure Mode\n    - 7B Severity\n    - 14B Severity\n    - Type\n    rows:\n    - - 'FM1: Global suppression'\n      - Catastrophic (retention 19.3%)\n      - Absent (retention >97%)\n      - 'Capacity-dependent: disappears'\n    - - 'FM2: Cross-dim interference'\n      - Strong (pol −25.6% rel)\n      - Weak (pol −8.0% rel)\n      - Partially attenuated\n    - - 'FM3: Overcorrection rebound'\n      - +7.2pp (4/4 runs)\n      - Absent (0/4 runs)\n      - 'Capacity-dependent: disappears'\n    - - 'FM4: DPO+BCP reversal'\n      - Strong (10/12, CI excl. 0)\n      - Attenuated (4/12, CI incl. 0)\n      - 'Capacity-dependent: attenuated'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scale-dependent failure severity heatmap (4×2 grid): rows = FM1-FM4, columns\n    = 7B/14B. Color-coded red (catastrophic) → orange (moderate) → yellow (weak) →\n    green (absent). At 7B: FM1 red, FM2 orange, FM3 red, FM4 red. At 14B: FM1 green,\n    FM2 yellow, FM3 green, FM4 yellow. Gradient runs consistently from severe-left\n    to mild-right, visualizing the unified scale-dependency pattern.\n\n    '\n  - 'FM4 reversal comparison panel: side-by-side violin plots of per-episode politeness\n    gap distributions at 7B and 14B DPO+BCP. 7B distribution clearly shifted positive\n    (reversed); 14B distribution centered near zero with wide spread. Horizontal dashed\n    line at zero separates correct/reversed direction. 95% CI annotations on each.\n\n    '\n  - 'Gap trajectory plot: x-axis = scale (7B, 14B), y-axis = mean politeness gap (pp).\n    Two lines: base BCP (weak negative gaps at both scales) and DPO+BCP (strong positive\n    at 7B, near-zero at 14B). Lines converge at 14B, demonstrating that DPO+BCP interaction\n    diminishes with scale while base BCP ineffectiveness persists.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'The 14B DPO result is the strongest possible outcome for the paper narrative.\n    It promotes FM4 from \"documented at single scale\" to \"confirmed scale-dependent,\"\n    completing the taxonomy: all four failure modes show capacity-dependent severity.\n\n    The updated story becomes: \"We document four calibration failure mechanisms, all\n    more severe at 7B. FM1 and FM3 disappear at 14B (catastrophic effects are capacity-gated).\n    FM2 and FM4 persist weakly but are no longer statistically significant at 14B.\n    Yet calibration remains ineffective at both scales (H2 fails at both). Scaling\n    is necessary for safety but insufficient for calibration.\"\n\n    This closes every obvious reviewer attack: (1) \"Would DPO work at larger scale?\"\n    — No, H2 still fails. (2) \"Is FM4 structural or capacity-dependent?\" — Capacity-\n    dependent, with statistical evidence. (3) \"Is your taxonomy just 7B artifacts?\"\n    — FM2 persists at 14B; the rest are confirmed capacity-dependent with clean scale\n    comparison. (4) \"What about combining DPO+BCP at scale?\" — Done; interaction vanishes\n    because BCP itself is ignored at 14B.\n\n    The safety-efficacy gap now generalizes across both calibration paradigms and\n    all four failure modes. Estimated acceptance probability for EMNLP Findings with\n    full plan_005 + plan_006 data: 70-75%, limited primarily by single model family\n    (Qwen2.5).'\n","numLines":444,"startLine":1,"totalLines":444}}}
